hadiths[295]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21614","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Amash narrating from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Habib ibn Himaz, from Abu Dharr, he said: We came with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and we alighted at Dhu al-Hulayfah. Some men hastened to Madinah, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, spent the night and we spent it with him. In the morning he asked about them, and it was said: They hastened to Madinah. So he said: They hastened to Madinah and the women. Yet they will leave it in its best state. Then he said: Would that I knew when a fire will emerge from Yemen from Mount al-Wiraq, by which the necks of camels kneeling at Busra will be lit as by daylight."
"21615","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith al-Bakri, from Habib ibn Hammad, from Abu Dharr, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he mentioned its meaning."
"21616","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Hakam ibn Nafi Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash informed us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Husayn, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Abu Dharr, he said: I used to serve the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then I would come to the mosque when I finished my work and lie down in it. One day the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to me while I was lying down and nudged me with his foot, so I sat up straight. He said to me: O Abu Dharr, what will you do when you are expelled from it. I said: I will return to the mosque of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and to my house. He said: What will you do when you are expelled. I said: Then I will take my sword and strike with it whoever expels me. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, placed his hand on my shoulder and said: Forgiveness, O Abu Dharr, three times. Rather you will submit with them wherever they lead you, and go along with them wherever they drive you, even to a black slave. Abu Dharr said: When I was exiled to al-Rabadhah, prayer was established and a black man who was in charge of the zakat camels stepped forward, and when he saw me he moved to go back and put me forward, so I said: Stay as you are, rather I submit to the command of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"21617","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Muan ibn Rifaa, from Abu Khalaf, from Anas ibn Malik, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Islam is docile, it is ridden only docilely."
"21618","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Bakhtari ibn Ubayd ibn Salman, from his father, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Two are better than one, and three are better than two, and four are better than three, so hold to the congregation, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will not gather my ummah except upon guidance."
"21619","Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us that Abu Salim al-Jayshani came to Abu Umayyah in his house and said: I heard Abu Dharr saying that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: When one of you loves his companion, let him come to him in his house and inform him that he loves him for Allah, and I have come to you in your house."
"21620","Yunus and Affan with the meaning narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Burd Abu al-Ala, Affan said: Burd Abu al-Ala informed us, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Ghudayf ibn al-Harith, that he passed by Umar ibn al-Khattab and he said: What a fine youth is Ghudayf. Then Abu Dharr met him and said: O my brother, seek forgiveness for me. He said: You are a companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and you are more entitled to seek forgiveness for me. So he said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab saying: What a fine youth is Ghudayf, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has struck truth upon the tongue of Umar and his heart. Affan said: Upon the tongue of Umar, he speaks with it."
"21621","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Abdullah ibn Hubayrah, Abu Tamim al-Jayshani informed me, he said: Abu Dharr informed me, he said: I was walking with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Other than the Dajjal is what I fear more for my ummah. He said it three times. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this other than the Dajjal that you fear more for your ummah. He said: Misguiding imams."
"21622","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Ibn Hubayrah, from Abu Tamim al-Jayshani, he said: I heard Abu Dharr saying: I was walking beside the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one day to his house, and I heard him saying: Other than the Dajjal is more fearful for my ummah than the Dajjal. When I feared he would enter, I said: O Messenger of Allah, what thing is more fearful for your ummah than the Dajjal. He said: The misguiding imams."
"21623","Ammar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: O Abu Dharr, shall I not guide you to a treasure among the treasures of Paradise: Say, there is no power nor strength except with Allah."
"21624","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Sulayman al-Amash narrated to me, from Mujahid ibn Jabr Abu al-Hajjaj, from Ubayd ibn Umayr al-Laythi, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was given five that no prophet before me was given: I was aided with terror, so the enemy fears me at a month journey; the earth was made for me a mosque and purification; war spoils were made lawful for me and were not lawful for anyone before me; I was sent to the red and the black; and it was said to me: Ask, you will be given, so I kept it hidden as intercession for my ummah, and it will reach among you, Allah willing, whoever meets Allah, Mighty and Majestic, not associating anything with Him. Al-Amash said: Mujahid used to hold that the red are mankind and the black are the jinn."
"21625","Muammal narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Salamah narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Dharr, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The sun disappears under the Throne and is permitted, so it returns. When it is that night whose morning it rises from the west, it will not be permitted. When morning comes it will be said to it: Rise from your place. Then he recited: Do they await except that the angels come to them, or your Lord comes, or some signs of your Lord come."
"21626","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever fasts three days of every month has fasted the whole lifetime."
"21627","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Daylam narrated to us, from Wahb ibn Abi Dubayy, from Abu Harb, from Mihjan, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The evil eye clings to a man by the permission of Allah until he climbs a high place then falls down from it."
"21628","Husayn narrated to us, Yazid meaning Ibn Ata narrated to us, from Yazid meaning Ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from a man, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us and said: Do you know which deeds are most beloved to Allah, Mighty and Majestic. One speaker said: Prayer and zakat, and another speaker said: Jihad. He said: The most beloved deeds to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, are love for Allah and hatred for Allah."
"21629","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from a man of Banu Amir, he said: I was a disbeliever, then Allah guided me to Islam, and I used to stay away from water with my family, and major impurity would befall me, and that weighed on my mind. Abu Dharr had been described to me, so I performed Hajj and entered the mosque of Mina and recognized him by the description: an elderly known dark-skinned man wearing a Qatari suit. So I went until I stood beside him while he was praying, and I greeted him and he did not return it to me. Then he prayed a prayer, completing it, perfecting it, and lengthening it. When he finished he returned it to me. I said: Are you Abu Dharr. He said: My family claim that. He said: I was a disbeliever, then Allah guided me to Islam, and my religion concerned me, and I used to stay away from water with my family, and major impurity would befall me, and that weighed on my mind. He said: Do you know Abu Dharr. I said: Yes. He said: I found Madinah uncongenial. Ayyub said, or a word like it. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered for me some camels and sheep, and I used to be among them, staying away from water with my family, and major impurity would befall me, and it weighed on my mind that I had perished. So I sat upon a camel of them and came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at midday while he was sitting in the shade of the mosque among a group of his Companions. I dismounted from the camel and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have perished. He said: And what has perished you. So I told him, and he laughed, then called a person of his household, and a black slave girl came with a large cup in it water, not full, shaking about. I concealed myself with the camel, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered a man of the people, so he screened me, and I bathed. Then I came to him and he said: Clean earth is purification as long as you do not find water, even for ten years; when you find water, touch your skin with it."
"21630","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from a man of Banu Qushayr, he said: I used to stay away from water, and major impurity would befall me, and I would not find water, so I would perform tayammum, and that weighed on my mind. So I came to Abu Dharr in his house and did not find him, then I came to the mosque, his appearance having been described to me, and there he was praying, so I recognized him by the description. I greeted him and he did not return to me until he finished, then he returned to me. So I said: Are you Abu Dharr. He said: My family claim that. So I said: There was no one among people more beloved to me to see than you. So he said: You have seen me. So I said: I used to stay away from water, and major impurity would befall me, and I remained days performing tayammum, and that weighed on my mind, or became problematic to me. So he said: Do you know Abu Dharr. I was in Madinah and found it uncongenial, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered for me a small flock of sheep, and I went out with it, and major impurity befell me, so I performed tayammum with earth and prayed days, and that weighed on my mind until I thought I had perished. So I ordered a she-camel or young camel of mine to be saddled, then I rode. He said: Until I came to Madinah and found the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the shade of the mosque among a group of his Companions. So I greeted him, and he raised his head and said: Glory be to Allah, Abu Dharr. So I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, major impurity befell me and I performed tayammum days, and that weighed on my mind until I thought I had perished. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called for water for me, and a black slave girl brought it in a large cup, shaking, so I concealed myself with the mount, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered a man, so he screened me, and I bathed. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Abu Dharr, clean earth is purification as long as you do not find water, even in ten years; when you are able to have water, touch it to your skin."
"21631","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Aliyah, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad delayed prayer, so I asked Abdullah ibn al-Samit, and he struck my thigh. He said: I asked my intimate friend Abu Dharr, and he struck my thigh and said: I asked my intimate friend, meaning the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Pray the prayer at its fixed time, and if you catch it with them, pray with them, and do not say: I have already prayed, so I will not pray."
"21632","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah al-Aslami, from Abu al-Aswad, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best with which you change this gray hair is henna and katam."
"21633","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Mukhariq, he said: We went out as pilgrims, and when we reached al-Rabadhah I said to my companions: Go ahead, and I stayed behind and came to Abu Dharr while he was praying. I saw him lengthening the standing and increasing bowing and prostration, so I mentioned that to him. So he said: I did my best to do well. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever bows a bowing or prostrates a prostration is raised a degree by it and a sin is removed from him by it."
"21634","He said: I read this hadith to my father and he affirmed it. Mahdi ibn Jafar al-Ramli narrated to me, Damrah narrated to me, from Abu Zurah al-Saybani, from Qanbar the chamberlain of Muawiyah, he said: Abu Dharr used to speak harshly to Muawiyah. He said: So he complained of him to Ubadah ibn al-Samit and to Abu al-Darda and to Amr ibn al-As and to Umm Haram. So he said: You have accompanied as he accompanied and seen as he saw, so if you see fit to speak to him. Then he sent to Abu Dharr, so he came, and they spoke to him. So he said: As for you, O Abu al-Walid, you embraced Islam before me, and you have age and merit over me, and I would have desired for you to avoid such a sitting. As for you, O Abu al-Darda, the death of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, almost passed you by, then you embraced Islam and were among the righteous Muslims. As for you, O Amr ibn al-As, you struggled with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. As for you, O Umm Haram, you are but a woman, and your intellect is the intellect of a woman. As for you and that. He said: So Ubadah said: Certainly I will never sit such a sitting again."
"21635","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, he said: And Buhayr ibn Sad informed me, from Khalid ibn Madan, he said: Abu Dharr said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He has succeeded who made his heart sincere for faith, and made his heart sound, his tongue truthful, his soul tranquil, his disposition straight, and made his ear listening and his eye seeing. As for the ear, it is a funnel, and the eye is a retainer for what the heart retains. And he has succeeded who made his heart retentive."
"21636","Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from al-Marur ibn Suwayd, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: O son of Adam, if you did sins nearly filling the earth and did not associate anything with Me, I would make for you forgiveness nearly filling it."
"21637","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Salim ibn Ghaylan, from Sulayman ibn Abi Uthman, from Adi ibn Hatim al-Himsi, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: My ummah will remain in good as long as they hasten breaking the fast and delay the sahur."
"21638","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, he said: I said to Abu Dharr: If I had seen the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I would have asked him. He said: And what would you have asked him. He said: I would have asked him whether he saw his Lord, Mighty and Majestic. He said: I did ask him, and he said: I saw Him, a light, how could I see Him."
"21639","Affan said: And it reached me from Ibn Hisham meaning Muadh that he narrated it from his father as Hammam said: I saw Him."
"21640","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Ubayd ibn Umayr al-Laythi, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was given five that no one before me was given: I was sent to the red and the black; the earth was made for me purification and a mosque; war spoils were made lawful for me and were not lawful for anyone before me; I was aided with terror, so the enemy fears while a month journey from me; and it was said to me: Ask, you will be given, and I kept my supplication hidden as intercession for my ummah, and it will reach among you, Allah Exalted willing, whoever does not associate anything with Allah."
"21641","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from al-Marur ibn Suwayd, that Abu Dharr said: The truthful one believed, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to us in what he narrates from his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, that He said: The good deed is for ten likes of it or more, and the evil deed is for one, or I forgive. If you met Me with sins nearly filling the earth, not associating with Me, I would meet you with forgiveness nearly filling it. He said: And qirab of the earth is the fill of the earth."
"21642","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Asim, from al-Marur ibn Suwayd, from Abu Dharr, he said: I heard the truthful one believed, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he mentioned its meaning."
"21643","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Mutarrif, he said: I sat with a group of Quraysh, then a man came and began praying, bowing and prostrating, then standing, then bowing and prostrating, not sitting. So I said: By Allah, I do not see this one knows whether he finishes on even or odd. So they said: Will you not stand to him and tell him. He said: So I stood and said: O servant of Allah, I do not see you know whether you finish on even or on odd. He said: But Allah knows. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever prostrates to Allah a prostration, Allah writes for him by it a good deed, removes by it from him a sin, and raises for him by it a degree. So I said: Who are you. So he said: Abu Dharr. So I returned to my companions and said: May Allah reward you with evil for companions, you ordered me to teach a man from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"21644","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Mudrik informed me, he said: I heard Abu Zurah narrating from Kharashah ibn al-Hurr, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Three whom Allah will not speak to, nor look at on the Day of Resurrection, nor purify, and for them is a painful punishment. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, who are they, they have lost and failed. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, repeated it three times. He said: The one who drags his garment, the one who promotes his goods with false or wicked oath, and the one who reminds of favors."
"21645","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Hasīrah narrated to us, Zayd ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Abu Dharr said: For me to swear ten times that Ibn Said is the Dajjal is more beloved to me than to swear once that he is not he. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me to his mother. He said: Ask her how long she carried him. He said: So I came to her and asked her, and she said: I carried him twelve months. He said: Then he sent me to her and said: Ask her about his cry when he fell. He said: So I returned to her and asked her, and she said: He cried the cry of a one-month-old boy. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: I have hidden for you something hidden. He said: You hid for me the snout of a dusty sheep and the smoke. He said: He wanted to say al-dukhan but could not, so he said: al-dukh al-dukh. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Be gone, for you will not exceed your measure."
"21646","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abu Masud al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu Abdullah al-Jasri, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked which speech is best. He said: What Allah, Mighty and Majestic, chose for His servants: Glory be to Allah and with His praise."
"21647","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Maruf, that Abu Dharr narrated to them that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If My servant meets Me with sins nearly filling the earth, I will meet him with forgiveness nearly filling it."
"21648","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Amr ibn Murrah informed me, from Suwayd ibn al-Harith, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: It would not please me to have Uhud as gold, dying the day I die while with me from it a dinar or half a dinar, except that I set it aside for a creditor."
"21649","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Humayd ibn Hilal informed me, he heard Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The prayer of a man is cut off when there is not before him like the back of a saddle: the woman, the donkey, and the black dog. I said: What is with the black rather than the red. He said: O son of my brother, I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as you asked me, and he said: The black dog is a devil."
"21650","Marhum ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Attar narrated to us, Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Abu Dharr, pray the prayer at its time, and if you come to the people while they have prayed, you have secured your prayer, and if they have not prayed, pray with them, and it will be voluntary for you."
"21651","Marhum narrated to us, Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rode a donkey and seated me behind him and said: O Abu Dharr, what if severe hunger afflicts people so you cannot rise from your bed to your mosque, what will you do. He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Restrain yourself. He said: O Abu Dharr, what if severe death afflicts people so that a house is for a slave, meaning the grave, what will you do. I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Be patient. He said: O Abu Dharr, what if people kill one another, meaning until the stones of oil become drowned in blood, what will you do. He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Sit in your house and close your door upon you. He said: If I am not left alone. He said: Then go to those whom you are from and be among them. He said: Shall I take my weapon. He said: Then you would share with them in what they are in, but if you fear the gleam of the sword dazzles you, cast the edge of your cloak over your face so he bears his sin and your sin."
"21652","Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: O Abu Dharr, when you cook, increase the broth and look after your neighbors, or share among your neighbors."
"21653","Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the vessels of the Hawd. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, its vessels are more than the number of stars of the sky and its planets on a dark clear night, vessels of Paradise. Whoever drinks from it will never thirst after it. Two spouts from Paradise pour into it. Whoever drinks from it will not thirst. Its width is like its length, between Amman and Aylah. Its water is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey."
"21654","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Fulayt al-Amiri narrated to me, from Jasrah al-Amiriyyah, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed a night and recited a verse until morning, bowing with it and prostrating with it: If You punish them, they are Your servants, and if You forgive them, You are the Mighty, the Wise. In the morning I said: O Messenger of Allah, you kept reciting this verse until morning, bowing with it and prostrating with it. He said: I asked my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, for intercession for my ummah, and He gave it to me, and it will reach, Allah willing, whoever does not associate anything with Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"21655","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Salim meaning Ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: O Abu Dharr, which mountain is this. I said: Uhud, O Messenger of Allah. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, it would not please me that it were gold for me in pieces, spending it in the path of Allah, leaving of it a qirat. He said: I said: A qintar, O Messenger of Allah. He said: A qirat, he said it three times. Then he said: O Abu Dharr, I only say what is less, and do not say what is more."
"21656","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abu Dharr, raising it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: When one of you stands for prayer, mercy faces him, so let him not wipe the pebbles."
"21657","Sufyan narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Murawih, from Abu Dharr, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best. He said: Faith in Allah Exalted and jihad in His path. I said: O Messenger of Allah, which necks are best. He said: The most precious to their owners and the dearest in price. He said: If I do not find. He said: You help a craftsman or make for one lacking skill. And he said: If I cannot. He said: Withhold your harm from people, for it is charity you give for yourself."
"21658","Harun narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, he said: I heard Abu al-Ahwas, freedman of Banu Layth, narrating to us in the gathering of Ibn al-Musayyab, with Ibn al-Musayyab sitting, that he heard Abu Dharr saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you stands for prayer, mercy faces him, so let him not move the pebbles, or not touch the pebbles."
"21659","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Dharr, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Which mosque was placed on earth first. He said: The Sacred Mosque. I said: Then which. He said: Then al-Masjid al-Aqsa. I said: How long between them. He said: Forty years. I said: Then which. He said: Then wherever you reach prayer, pray, for all of it is a mosque."
"21660","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: We heard it from two and three. Hakim ibn Jubayr narrated to us, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Ibn al-Hawtakiyyah, he said: Umar said: Who of us was present on the day of al-Qahah. So Abu Dharr said: I was. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded him to fast the white bright days: thirteen, fourteen, and fifteen."
"21661","Sufyan narrated to us, two narrated to us, from Musa ibn Talhah: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman and Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Ibn al-Hawtakiyyah, from Abu Dharr, that he said: A man said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he commanded him to fast thirteen, fourteen, and fifteen."
"21662","Sufyan narrated to us, he heard Muhammad ibn al-Saib ibn Barakah, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Dharr, he said: I was walking behind the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Shall I not guide you to a treasure among the treasures of Paradise. I said: Yes. He said: There is no power nor strength except with Allah."
"21663","Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Ajlah, from Ibn Buraydah, from Abu al-Aswad al-Dili, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Among the best with which you changed gray hair are henna and katam."
"21664","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah al-Aslami, from Abu al-Aswad, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Among the best with which gray hair was changed are henna and katam."
"21665","Ismail narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Salil, from Nuaym ibn Qanab al-Riyahi, he said: I came to Abu Dharr and did not find him, and I saw the woman, so I asked her, and she said: He is there in a property of his. Then he came leading or driving two camels, one tied behind the other, with a waterskin on the neck of each. He put down the two waterskins. I said: O Abu Dharr, there was no one among people more beloved to me to meet than you, nor more hateful to me to meet than you. He said: May Allah bless your father, what combines this. He said: I said: I used to bury alive in Jahiliyyah, and I hoped in meeting you that you would inform me that I have repentance and a way out, and I feared in meeting you that you would inform me that I have no repentance. So he said: Was it in Jahiliyyah. I said: Yes. So he said: Allah has pardoned what passed. Then he turned his head to the woman and ordered food for me, and she resisted him, then he ordered her and she resisted him until their voices rose. He said: Leave us alone, for you women will not exceed what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to us about you. I said: And what did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say to you about them. He said: Woman is a rib; if you go to straighten her you break her, and if you leave her, in her is crookedness and sufficiency. So she went and brought a tharid like a sandgrouse. So he said: Eat, and let it not alarm you, I am fasting. Then he stood praying, refining the bowing and lightening it, and I saw him aiming that I eat to full or near. Then he came and put his hand with me. So I said: To Allah we belong and to Him we return. So he said: What is with you. So I said: Whom I feared among people would lie to me, I did not fear you would lie to me. He said: May Allah bless your father, if I lied to you a lie since I met you. So he said: Did you not inform me that you are fasting, then I see you eating. He said: Yes, I fasted three days of this month, so its reward became due for me, and food became lawful for me with you."
"21666","Ismail narrated to us, al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu al-Ala ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Ibn al-Ahmasi, he said: I met Abu Dharr and said to him: It reached me from you that you narrate a hadith from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So he said: Yet do not think I lie upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, after I heard it from him. So what reached you from me. I said: It reached me that you say: Three whom Allah loves and three whom Allah, Mighty and Majestic, hates. He said: I said it and heard it. I said: Who are these whom Allah loves. He said: A man meeting the enemy in the detachment, offering his neck to them until he is killed or victory is opened for his companions; people traveling, their night journey lengthening until they wish to touch the ground, so they alight, then one of them withdraws and prays until he awakens them for their departure; and a man having a neighbor harming him with his neighborhood, enduring his harm until death or departure separates them. I said: And who are these whom Allah hates. He said: The swearing trader, or he said the swearing seller, the miserly favor-reminder, and the poor arrogant."
"21667","Ismail narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Sasaa ibn Muawiyah, he said: I came to Abu Dharr. I said: What is with you. He said to me: My work. I said: Narrate to me. He said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No two Muslims whose three children die before reaching puberty except Allah forgives them. I said: Narrate to me. He said: Yes."
"21668","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No Muslim who spends a pair of every property of his in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, except the keepers of Paradise receive him, all of them calling him to what is with them. I said: And how is that. He said: If they were men, two men, and if camels, two camels, and if cattle, two cows."
"21669","Ismail narrated to us, from Yunus, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abdullah ibn Samit, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you stands praying, he is screened when before him is like the back of a saddle; if there is not before him like the back of a saddle, his prayer is cut off by the donkey, the woman, and the black dog. I said: O Abu Dharr, what is with the black dog rather than the red dog rather than the yellow dog. He said: O son of my brother, I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as you asked me, and he said: The black dog is a devil."
"21670","Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from one who narrated to him, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was given them from a treasure from a house under the Throne, and no prophet before me was given them, meaning the two verses from the end of Surat al-Baqarah."
"21671","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Hirash, he said: Mansur from Zayd ibn Zabyan or from a man or from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was given the seals of Surat al-Baqarah from a treasure house from under the Throne, no prophet before me was given them."
"21672","Husayn narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribiy, from Kharashah ibn al-Hurr, from al-Marur ibn Suwayd, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was given the seals of Surat al-Baqarah from a treasure house from under the Throne, and no prophet before me was given them."
"21673","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Sulayman narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Shall I not guide you to a treasure among the treasures of Paradise: There is no power nor strength except with Allah."
"21674","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abu Dharr, he said: I was walking with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the lava field of Madinah in the evening while we looked at Uhud, and he said: O Abu Dharr. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I would not love that Uhud were gold with me, remaining to the third night with me from it a dinar, except a dinar I set aside for a debt, except that I say with it among the servants of Allah thus, and he scattered to his right, before him, and to his left. He said: Then we walked, and he said: O Abu Dharr, the wealthy are the fewest on the Day of Resurrection, except one who says thus and thus and thus, and he scattered to his right, before him, and to his left. He said: Then we walked, and he said: O Abu Dharr, stay as you are until I come to you. He said: So he went until he was hidden from me. He said: I heard noise and a voice. He said: So I said: Perhaps something happened to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So I was about to follow him, then I remembered his saying: Do not move until I come to you, so I waited for him until he came. I mentioned to him what I heard, and he said: That was Jibril, peace be upon him, he came to me and said: Whoever of your ummah dies not associating anything with Allah enters Paradise. He said: I said: Even if he fornicates and steals. He said: Even if he fornicates and steals."
"21675","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad, from Abu al-Aswad, from Abu Dharr, he said: He used to water at his pond, then people came, and he said: Which of you will water for Abu Dharr and count hairs of his head. A man said: I will. So the man came and watered his pond, then broke it. Abu Dharr was standing, then sat, then lay down. It was said to him: O Abu Dharr, why did you sit then lie down. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to us: When one of you angers while standing, let him sit; if anger leaves him, otherwise let him lie down."
"21676","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Talq ibn Habib, from Bushayr ibn Kab al-Adawi, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Do you want a treasure from the treasure of Paradise. I said: Yes. He said: There is no power nor strength except with Allah."
"21677","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sam, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever of you is fasting three days of the month, let him fast the three white days."
"21678","Muhammad ibn Ubayd and Ibn Numayr with the meaning narrated to us, they said: al-Amash narrated to us, from al-Marur ibn Suwayd, from Abu Dharr, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in the shade of the Kaaba, and he said: They are the greatest losers, by the Lord of the Kaaba, they are the greatest losers, by the Lord of the Kaaba. So grief seized me and I began breathing. He said: I said: This is an evil that happened in me. He said: I said: Who are they, may my father and mother be ransom for you. He said: The wealthy, except one who says among the servants of Allah thus and thus and thus, and few are they. There is no man who dies leaving sheep or camels or cattle without paying its zakat except it comes on the Day of Resurrection in its greatest and fattest form, trampling him with its hooves and goring him with its horns until judgment is passed among people, then its first returns upon its last. And Ibn Numayr said: Whenever its last is spent, its first returns upon him."
"21679","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Dharr, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the mosque when the sun set, and he said: O Abu Dharr, do you know where the sun goes. I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: It goes until it prostrates before its Lord, Mighty and Majestic, then seeks permission to return, and it is permitted. As if it was said to it: Return from where you came, so it returns to its rising place, and that is its resting place. Then he recited: And the sun runs to its resting place."
"21680","Abu Said narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abu Dharr, he said: While the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was preaching, a rude Bedouin stood to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, the hyena has eaten us. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Other than that is more fearful for you to me, when the world is poured upon you abundantly. Would that my ummah not adorn themselves with gold."
"21681","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Abu Dharr, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Fear Allah wherever you are, follow the evil deed with the good deed, it erases it, and mix with people with good character. Waki said: And Sufyan said once, from Muadh, but I found in my book, from Abu Dharr, and it is the first hearing."
"21682","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, he said: I heard Ribiy ibn Hirash narrating from Zayd ibn Zabyan, raised to Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Three whom Allah loves and three whom Allah hates. As for the three whom Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves: a man who came to people and asked them by Allah, not asking them by kinship between them, and they refused him, then a man stayed behind them and gave him secretly, none knowing his gift except Allah and the one he gave; people who traveled their night until, when sleep became dearer to them than what equals it, they alighted and laid their heads, then he stood cajoling Me and reciting My verses; and a man in a detachment meeting the enemy, defeated, then advancing with his chest until killed or Allah opens for him. And the three whom Allah hates: the old adulterer, the poor arrogant, and the rich unjust."
"21683","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribiy ibn Hirash, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves three and hates three. He hates the old adulterer, the poor arrogant, and the much-hoarding miser, and He loves three: a man in a squadron who charges protecting them until killed or Allah opens for him; a man among people who journeyed at night, then alighted at the end of night, sleep being dearer to them than what equals it, so they slept, and he stood reciting My verses and cajoling Me; and a man among people, then a man came asking them by kinship between him and them, and they were miserly to him, and he stayed behind them and gave him where none sees him except Allah and the one he gave."
"21684","Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribiy, from a man, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah hates, and he mentioned the hadith."
"21685","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Qurrah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Sasaa ibn Muawiyah, he said: I met Abu Dharr at al-Rabadhah. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever spends a pair of his property in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, the keepers of Paradise hasten to him."
"21686","And he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: No two Muslims whose three children die before reaching puberty except Allah enters them into Paradise by His mercy to them."
"21687","al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar, that Abu Abd al-Rahman informed him, from Abu Dharr, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: If a man passes by a door with no curtain over it, not closed, and looks, there is no sin upon him; the sin is only upon the people of the house."
"21688","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from al-Marur ibn Suwayd, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: Whoever does a good deed has ten likes of it or more, and whoever does an evil deed, its recompense is its like, or I forgive. Whoever does sins nearly filling the earth then meets Me not associating anything with Me, I make for him forgiveness like it. Whoever draws near to Me a span, I draw near to him a cubit; whoever draws near to Me a cubit, I draw near to him a fathom; whoever comes to Me walking, I come to him hastening."
"21689","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Mundhir, elderly men of Taym narrated to us, they said: Abu Dharr said: Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, left us, and no bird moves its wings in the sky except he mentioned to us knowledge from it."
"21690","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Ajlah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from Abu al-Aswad al-Dili, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best with which gray hair is changed are henna and katam."
"21691","Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Dharr, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, the rich have gone with the reward, praying, fasting, and performing Hajj. He said: And you pray, fast, and perform Hajj. I said: They give charity and we do not give charity. He said: And in you is charity: your removing bones from the road is charity; your guiding the road is charity; your helping the weak with your strength is charity; your expression for the speech-impaired is charity; your intercourse with your wife is charity. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we satisfy our desire and are rewarded. He said: What if you placed it in unlawful, would you sin. He said: I said: Yes. He said: So you count evil, and do you not count good."
"21692","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, from a man of Banu Tamim, he said: We were at the door of Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, with Abu Dharr among us. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Fasting the month of patience and three days of every month is fasting the lifetime, and removes the rancor of the chest. He said: I said: And what is the rancor of the chest. He said: The filth of Satan."
"21693","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Mabad ibn Hilal, a man in the mosque of Damascus narrated to me, from Awf ibn Malik, from Abu Dharr, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, what is fasting. He said: An obligatory sufficient one."
"21694","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Ribiy, from Kharashah ibn al-Hurr, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he took his bed at night, said: O Allah, in Your name we die and live. When he awoke he said: Praise be to Allah who gave us life after He made us die, and to Him is the resurrection."
"21695","Ammar ibn Muhammad ibn Ukht Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: O My servants, all of you are sinners except whom I protect, so seek My forgiveness, I forgive you. Whoever knows that I am able to forgive and seeks My forgiveness by My power, I forgive him and do not care. All of you are astray except whom I guide, so seek guidance from Me, I guide you. All of you are poor except whom I enrich, so ask Me, I enrich you. If your first and your last, your living and your dead, your moist and your dry, gathered upon the most wretched heart of My servants, it would not decrease from My kingdom the wing of a gnat. If they gathered upon the most pious heart of a servant of Mine, it would not increase in My kingdom the wing of a gnat. If your first and your last, your living and your dead, your moist and your dry, gathered and every asker of them asked Me what his wish reaches, and I gave every asker of them what he asked, it would not decrease Me, as if one of you passed by the shore of the sea and dipped a needle in it then pulled it out. Likewise that does not decrease from My kingdom, for I am Generous, Glorious, Eternal. My giving is speech and My punishment is speech. When I intend a thing I only say to it: Be, so it is."
"21696","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, Shahr narrated to us, Ibn Ghanm narrated to me that Abu Dharr narrated to him, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: O My servant, as long as you worship Me and hope in Me, I forgive you for what is in you. O My servant, if you meet Me with sins nearly filling the earth, not associating with Me, I meet you with forgiveness nearly filling it. Abu Dharr said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: O My servants, all of you are sinners except whom I protect, and he mentioned the like of it, except that he said: That is because I am Generous, Finding, Glorious. My giving is but speech."
"21697","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abu Dharr, he said: A Bedouin stood to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, the hyena has eaten us, meaning the year of drought. He said: Other than that is more fearful for you to me: the world when poured upon you abundantly. Would that my ummah not wear gold."
"21698","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Ayyub al-Sikhtiyani and Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, each mentioned it, Khalid from Amr ibn Bujdan and Ayyub from a man, from Abu Dharr, that Abu Dharr came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while junub, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called for water for him, and he concealed himself and bathed. Then he said to him: Clean earth is the ablution of the Muslim even if he does not find water ten years; when he finds water, let him touch it to his skin, for that is better."
"21699","Muammal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Hajjaj al-Aswad narrated to us, Muammal said, and he was a righteous man, he said: I heard Abu al-Siddiq narrating to Thabit al-Bunani, from a man, from Abu Dharr, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You are in a time whose scholars are many and whose preachers are few; whoever abandons a tenth of what he knows perishes, or he said is ruined. There will come upon people a time its scholars few and its preachers many; whoever holds to a tenth of what he knows is saved."
"21700","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Uthman, from Mujahid, from Ibrahim ibn al-Ashtar, from his father, from Umm Dharr, she said: When death came to Abu Dharr, she said: I wept. So he said: What makes you weep. She said: How should I not weep while you die in a desert land, and I have no means to bury you, and I have no garment large enough for you to shroud you in. He said: Do not weep, and rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: No two Muslim women lose two or three children and endure patiently or seeking reward, then ever enter the Fire."
"21701","And indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A man from among you will surely die in a deserted land of the earth, witnessed by a company of believers, and there is none of those men but he has already died in a village or a community, and indeed I am the one who will die in a deserted land; by Allah, I have not lied nor been lied to."
"21702","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Amr, from Yazid ibn Nuaym, he said: I heard Abu Dharr al-Ghifari while he was upon the minbar at al-Fustat saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever draws near to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, a span, He draws near to him a cubit, and whoever draws near to Allah a cubit, He draws near to him a fathom, and whoever comes to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, walking, Allah comes to him hastening; and Allah is Most High and Most Glorious; and Allah is Most High and Most Glorious."
"21703","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar, from al-Himsi, from Abu Talib, from Abu Dharr, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever falsely accuses a slave girl he did not see committing adultery, Allah will flog him on the Day of Resurrection with a whip of fire."
"21704","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Muhajir Abu al-Hasan, he said: I heard Zayd ibn Wahb saying: We came from a funeral and passed by Abu Dharr, and he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and the caller to prayer wanted to call the adhan for Zuhr, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cool it down, then he wanted to call the adhan and he said to him: Cool it down, and the third time, Shubah said to the best of my knowledge he said to him, until we saw the shade of the hillocks; he said: The intensity of heat is from the blaze of Hell, so when the heat is intense, cool down the prayer."
"21705","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Asim, from al-Marur ibn Suwayd, from Abu Dharr, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the truthful, the believed, saying: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: The good deed is ten or more, and the evil deed is one or I forgive it; so whoever meets Me associating nothing with Me, with near the earth in sin, I make for him the like of it in forgiveness."
"21706","Bahz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, he said: The prayer of a man is cut off, if there is not before him the like of the back of a saddle, by the woman and the donkey and the black dog; he said: I said to Abu Dharr: What is the matter with the black dog as distinct from the red dog? He said: O son of my brother, I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as you asked me, and he said: The black dog is a devil."
"21707","Bahz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, he said: Abu Dharr said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man loves the people but cannot do their deeds; he said: You, O Abu Dharr, are with whom you loved; he said: I said: For I love Allah and His Messenger, repeating it once or twice."
"21708","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, a man does a deed and the people praise him for it and laud him for it; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is the hastened glad tidings of the believer."
"21709","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abu Imran informed us, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined me, when I cook a pot, to increase its broth, for it reaches the neighbours more."
"21710","Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad al-Dili, from his uncle, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me while I was sleeping in the mosque of Madinah, and he struck me with his foot and said: Do I not see you sleeping in it? He said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, my eye overcame me; he said: What will you do when you are expelled from it? He said: I shall go to Sham, the sacred, blessed land; he said: What will you do when you are expelled from it? He said: What shall I do, O Prophet of Allah, I shall strike with my sword; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not guide you to what is better than that and nearer to right guidance: You hear and obey and follow them wherever they drive you."
"21711","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, he said: I used to recite to him and he would recite to me in the lane, and he would pass by a prostration and prostrate; he said: I said: Do you prostrate in the lane? He said: Yes, I heard Abu Dharr saying: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which mosque was placed on the earth first? He said: The Sacred Mosque; he said: I said: Then which? He said: Then al-Masjid al-Aqsa; he said: I said: How many years between them? He said: Forty years; he said: Then wherever the prayer reaches you, pray, for it is a mosque; and Abu Awanah said: I used to read to him and he would read to me."
"21712","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, that he was with Abu Dharr, and his stipend came out, and with him was a slave girl of his, and she began to settle his needs; he said: Seven remained with her, so he ordered her to buy small coins with it; he said: I said to him: If only you had saved it for a need that befalls you or for a guest who alights with you; he said: My friend enjoined me that any gold or silver that is tied up is an ember upon its owner until he spends it in the cause of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"21713","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Yahya, Abu Salih narrated to me, from a man of Banu Asad, and Yala narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Dhakwan Abu Salih, from a man of Banu Asad, that Abu Dharr informed him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most intense of my nation in love for me are a people who will be, or will emerge, after me; one of them wishes that he had given his family and his wealth and that he had seen me."
"21714","Yahya narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from Abu al-Aswad, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The best of what grey hair is changed with is henna and katam."
"21715","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no might nor power except with Allah is a treasure from the treasures of Paradise."
"21716","Waki narrated to us, Fulan al-Amiri narrated to us, from Jasrah bint Dajajah, from Abu Dharr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse and repeated it until morning: If You punish them, then they are Your servants, and if You forgive them, then You are the Mighty, the Wise."
"21717","Waki narrated to us, from Shubah, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray the prayer at its time."
"21718","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Dharr, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which mosque was placed first? He said: The Sacred Mosque; he said: I said: Then which? He said: Then al-Masjid al-Aqsa; he said: I said: How many years between them? He said: Forty years; then wherever the prayer reaches you, pray, for it is a mosque."
"21719","Ubaydah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, and he mentioned it, except that he said: Which mosque was placed on the earth first."
"21720","Waki and Bahz narrated to us, they said: Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Qatadah, Bahz said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, he said: I said to Abu Dharr: If I had met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) I would have asked him; he said: About what? I said: Did you see your Lord? So he said: I did ask him, and he said: Light, how could I see Him, meaning in the affirmative manner."
"21721","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from al-Marur ibn Suwayd, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and it will be said: Present to him his minor sins; he said: So they will be presented to him and his major ones hidden from him, and it will be said: You did on such and such a day such and such, and he will be confessing, not denying, and he will be fearful of the major ones, and it will be said: Give him in place of every evil deed a good deed; he said: Then he will say: Indeed I have sins I do not see; he said: Abu Dharr said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laugh until his molars appeared."
"21722","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and Yala narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise: There is no might nor power except with Allah."
"21723","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and Yala narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise: There is no might nor power except with Allah."
"21724","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Mushir, from Kharashah ibn al-Hurr, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abu Dharr, look at the highest man in the mosque; he said: So I looked, and there was a man upon him a fine suit; he said: I said: This one; he said: He said to me: Look at the lowest man in the mosque; he said: So I looked, and there was a man upon him worn clothes; he said: I said: This one; he said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This one is better with Allah on the Day of Resurrection than an earth-full of the like of this one."
"21725","Ibn Numayr and Yala narrated to us, they said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abu Dharr, he said: I was walking with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque, and he said: O Abu Dharr, raise your head and look at the highest man in the mosque, then he mentioned the hadith."
"21726","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abu Dharr, and he mentioned the hadith, and he said: Better with Allah than an earth-full of the like of this one, and such; Muawiyah ibn Amr said: From Zayd."
"21727","And Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, Sulayman ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Kharashah, and he mentioned it."
"21728","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from al-Marur ibn Suwayd, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: The most numerous are the lowest on the Day of Resurrection, except whoever says with wealth thus and thus and thus and thus, and few are they."
"21729","Waki and Ibn Jafar narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, Ibn Jafar said: I heard Abu Imran, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, the son of the brother of Abu Dharr, and Abu Dharr was his uncle, from Abu Dharr, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, what of a man who does a deed and the people love him for it? He said: That is the hastened glad tidings of the believer."
"21730","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from al-Marur ibn Suwayd, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no owner of camels nor cattle nor sheep who does not pay its zakat but they will come on the Day of Resurrection the greatest and fattest they ever were, butting him with their horns and trampling him with their hooves; whenever the last of them passes, the first of them returns upon him, until judgment is passed between the people."
"21731","Waki narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the jet-black dog; so he said: A devil."
"21732","Waki and Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib, from Maymun, from Abu Dharr, Abd al-Rahman said: He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me; he said: Fear Allah wherever you are, and follow the evil deed with the good deed, it wipes it out, and mix with the people with good character; my father said: And Waki had narrated it to us from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Muadh, then he retracted."
"21733","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from a man, from Kharashah, from Abu Dharr, and al-Masudi, from Ali ibn Mudrik, from Kharashah, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Three, Allah will not speak to them on the Day of Resurrection, nor look at them, nor purify them, and for them is a painful torment; I said: O Messenger of Allah, who are they, for they have failed and lost; he said: The one who reminds of his giving, and the one who drags his lower garment, and the one who promotes his goods with a wicked oath."
"21734","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Dharr, he said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about His saying, Exalted is He: And the sun runs to its resting place; he said: Its resting place is beneath the Throne."
"21735","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Sulayman ibn Mushir, from Kharashah ibn al-Hurr, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, then he mentioned the hadith; Ibn Jafar said: The one who reminds of what he gave, and the one who drags his lower garment."
"21736","Waki narrated to us, from Abu Hilal, from Bakr, from Abu Dharr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Look, for you are not better than a red man nor a black man except that you excel him with piety."
"21737","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, and Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash, from Sulayman ibn Mushir, from Kharashah ibn al-Hurr, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Three, Allah will not speak to them: The one who reminds, who gives nothing but reminds of it, and the one who drags his lower garment, and the one who promotes his goods with a wicked oath."
"21738","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Wasil, from al-Marur, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Your brothers, Allah has made them a trial under your hands; so whoever has his brother under his hand, let him feed him from his food and clothe him from his clothing, and not burden him with what overcomes him; and if he burdens him with what overcomes him, let him help him with it."
"21739","Waki narrated to us, from Umar ibn Dharr, he said: Mujahid said, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah sent no prophet except with the language of his people."
"21740","Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Umar ibn Said, from Bishr ibn Asim, from Asim, Abdullah ibn al-Harith said: His father, from Abu Dharr, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, the companions of wealth and riches have clearly outstripped us; they pray and fast as we pray and fast, and they have wealth with which they give charity, and we have no wealth; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of a deed, if you take to it you will reach those who were before you and surpass those who will be after you, except one who takes to the like of your deed: You glorify Allah after every prayer thirty-three times, and praise thirty-three times, and magnify thirty-four times."
"21741","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from al-Marur ibn Suwayd, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting in the shade of the Kabah; he said: So I came, and when he saw me he said: They are the losers, by the Lord of the Kabah; so I sat, and I could not remain till I stood up to him and said: Who are they, may my father and mother ransom you; he said: They are the most numerous in wealth, except whoever says with wealth thus and thus and thus, and few are they."
"21742","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Qurrah, al-Hasan narrated to us, Sasaa ibn Muawiyah narrated to me, he said: I reached al-Rabadhah, and there was Abu Dharr, he had met me with riding camels he had watered then issued, and he had hung a waterskin on the neck of a camel among them for him to drink and to water his companions, and it was a custom from the customs of the Arabs; I said: O Abu Dharr, how are you? He said to me: My deeds; I said: Tell, O Abu Dharr, what did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever spends a pair of his wealth, the keepers of Paradise hasten to him; we said: What are these two pairs? He said: If they are riding animals, then two mounts, and if they are horses, then two horses, and if they are camels, then two camels, until he counted all the kinds of wealth."
"21743","I said: O Abu Dharr, tell, what did you hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There are no two Muslims whose three children die before reaching puberty but Allah admits them to Paradise by virtue of His mercy for the calamity."
"21744","Affan narrated to us, Mahdi narrated to us, Wasil al-Ahdab narrated to us, from Marur ibn Suwayd, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I heard him saying: There came to me a comer from my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and he informed me, or he said: He gave me glad tidings, Mahdi doubted, that whoever dies of my nation associating nothing with Allah enters Paradise; I said: Even if he commits adultery and steals? He said: Even if he commits adultery and steals."
"21745","Affan narrated to us, Sallam Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Wasi, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, he said: My friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me with seven: He commanded me with love of the poor and nearness to them, and commanded me to look to one who is below me and not to look to one who is above me, and commanded me to join kinship though it turns away, and commanded me not to ask anyone for anything, and commanded me to speak the truth though it be bitter, and commanded me not to fear in Allah the blame of a blamer, and commanded me to increase saying: There is no might nor power except with Allah, for they are from a treasure beneath the Throne."
"21746","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma, that he entered upon Abu Dharr while he was at al-Rabadhah, and with him was a black, hungry wife of his, upon whom was no trace of finery nor perfume; he said: So he said: Will you not look at what this little black woman orders me with: She orders me to go to Iraq, and if I go to Iraq they will incline upon me with their worldly life; and my friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined me that before the bridge of Hell is a road with slip and stumbling, and we shall come upon it with our loads light, and Matar also narrated the hadith in full, in the saying of one of them: That we come upon it with our loads light, and the other said: That we come upon it with our loads light, and the other said: That we come upon it with our loads constrained, it is more likely to save us than that we come upon it while we are heavily laden."
"21747","Hashim narrated to us, al-Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Abu Naamah, Ubaydullah ibn al-Samit narrated to me, from Abu Dharr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Dharr, there will be over you leaders who kill the prayer; so if you reach them, pray the prayer at its time, and make your prayers with them supererogatory."
"21748","Husayn narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, Abu Naamah narrated to me, Abdullah ibn al-Samit narrated to me, that Abu Dharr said to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Dharr, there will be leaders, then he mentioned the hadith."
"21749","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Dawud, from al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Abu Dharr, he said: We fasted with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Ramadan, and he did not lead us in anything of the month until, when it was the night of twenty-four, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood with us until a third of the night had nearly gone; then when it was the following night he did not lead us; then when it was the night of twenty-six, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood with us until half the night had nearly gone; he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you had supererogated for us the rest of this night of ours; he said: No, when a man stands with the imam until he leaves, standing the night is counted for him; then when it was the following night he did not lead us; then when it was the night of twenty-eight, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered his family and the people gathered for him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with us until we nearly missed al-Falah; he said: I said: What is al-Falah? He said: The suhur; then he did not lead us, O son of my brother, in anything of the month."
"21750","Abd al-Rahman and Abd al-Samad with the same meaning narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, Abd al-Samad said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma, and Abd al-Samad said: al-Rahabi, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in what he narrates from his Lord, Mighty and Majestic: I have forbidden injustice upon Myself and upon My servants, so do not wrong one another; every son of Adam errs by night and day, then he seeks My forgiveness, so I forgive him and I do not care; and He said: O sons of Adam, all of you were astray except whom I guided, and all of you were naked except whom I clothed, and all of you were hungry except whom I fed, and all of you were thirsty except whom I gave drink; so seek guidance from Me, I shall guide you, and seek clothing from Me, I shall clothe you, and seek food from Me, I shall feed you, and seek drink from Me, I shall give you drink; O My servants, if the first of you and the last of you, and your jinn and your men, and your young and your old, and your male and your female, Abd al-Samad said: And your Bedouins and your sons, were upon the heart of the most pious single man among you, you would add nothing in My dominion; and if the first of you and the last of you, and your jinn and your men, and your young and your old, and your male and your female, were upon the heart of the most disbelieving single man, you would decrease nothing from My dominion except as the head of a needle decreases from the sea."
"21751","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Dharr, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which mosque was placed on the earth first? He said: The Sacred Mosque; he said: I said: Then which? He said: Then al-Masjid al-Aqsa; Abu Muawiyah said: Meaning Bayt al-Maqdis; he said: I said: How many years between them? He said: Forty years; and wherever the prayer reaches you, pray, for it is a mosque."
"21752","My father said, and Ibn Jafar: Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Ibrahim al-Taymi, and he mentioned its meaning."
"21753","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu al-Aliyah al-Barra, he said: Ibn Ziyad delayed the prayer, then Abdullah ibn al-Samit came to me, so I laid for him a cushion and he sat upon it, and I mentioned to him the deed of Ibn Ziyad, so he bit upon his lip and struck my thigh and said: I asked Abu Dharr as you asked me, and he struck my thigh as I struck your thigh, and he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as you asked me, and he struck my thigh as I struck your thigh, and he said: Pray the prayer at its time, and if you reach it with them, then pray, and do not say: I have prayed and I shall not pray."
"21754","Ismail narrated to us, from Yunus, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you stands praying, he is screened if there is before him the like of the back of a saddle; and if there is not before him the like of the back of a saddle, then his prayer is cut off by the donkey and the woman and the black dog; he said: So I said: O Abu Dharr, what is the matter with the black dog as distinct from the red dog, from the yellow dog? So he said: O son of my brother, I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as you asked me, and he said: The black dog is a devil."
"21755","Ismail narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ala ibn al-Shikhkhir, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, he said: I arrived in Madinah, and while I was in a circle in which were chiefs of Quraysh, a man came and mentioned the hadith, so I followed him until he sat at a pillar, and I said: I saw these only disliked what you said to them; so he said: My friend Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me and said: O Abu Dharr, so I answered him, and he said: Do you see Uhud? So I looked at what sun was upon it, while I thought he would send me for a need, and I said: I see it; he said: It would not please me to have the like of it in gold, I spend it all except three dinars."
"21756","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Suwayd ibn al-Harith, he said: I heard Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I would not love to have the like of Uhud in gold, Shubah said: Or he said: I would not love to have Uhud in gold, I leave from it on the day I die a dinar or half a dinar except for a creditor."
"21757","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he mentioned things for which a man is rewarded until he mentioned to me approaching his wife; so they said: O Messenger of Allah, is he rewarded in his desire he fulfils? He said: Do you see, if he were sinful, would there not be burden upon him? So they said: Yes; he said: Likewise he is rewarded."
"21758","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Imran, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, he said: My friend, peace be upon him, enjoined me with three: Hear and obey, even for a slave with mutilated limbs, and when you make broth, increase its water, then look at a household of your neighbours and give them from it with kindness, and pray the prayer at its time, and if you find the imam has prayed, you have secured your prayer, otherwise it is supererogatory."
"21759","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: I heard Shubah, from Abu Masud, from Abu Abdullah al-Jasri, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The most beloved speech to Allah is for the servant to say: Glory be to Allah and with His praise; Hajjaj said: He asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the most beloved deed to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, or the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved speech to Allah is: Glory be to Allah and with His praise."
"21760","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The prayer is cut off, if there is not before the man the like of the back of a saddle, by the woman and the donkey and the black dog; so I said: What is the matter with the black as distinct from the red? So he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as you asked me, and he said: The black is a devil."
"21761","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Wasil al-Ahdab informed me, he said: I heard al-Marur ibn Suwayd, he said: I met Abu Dharr at al-Rabadhah, and upon him was a garment and upon his boy was a garment, then he mentioned its meaning, that is, the meaning of the hadith after it."
"21762","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Wasil al-Ahdab, from al-Marur ibn Suwayd, he said: Hajjaj said: I heard al-Marur, he said: I saw Abu Dharr, and upon him was a fine suit, Hajjaj said: At al-Rabadhah, and upon his boy was the like of it, Hajjaj said: Another time, so I asked him about that, and he mentioned that he reviled a man at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and shamed him by his mother; he said: So the man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: You are a man in whom is ignorance; your brothers are your servants, Allah has placed them under your hands, so whoever has his brother under his hand, let him feed him from what he eats and clothe him from what he wears, and do not burden them with what overcomes them; and if you burden them, then help them with it."
"21763","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Wasil al-Ahdab, from al-Marur, he said: I heard Abu Dharr narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and gave me glad tidings, and he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abu Dharr al-Ghifari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Jibril, peace be upon him, gave me glad tidings that whoever dies of your nation associating nothing with Allah enters Paradise; he said: I said: Even if he commits adultery and steals? He said: Even if he commits adultery and steals."
"21764","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Wasil al-Ahdab, from al-Marur, he said: I heard Abu Dharr narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and gave me glad tidings, and he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abu Dharr al-Ghifari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Jibril, peace be upon him, gave me glad tidings that whoever dies of your nation associating nothing with Allah enters Paradise; he said: I said: Even if he commits adultery and steals? He said: Even if he commits adultery and steals."
"21765","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Bahz and Hajjaj narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Wasil, Bahz said: Wasil al-Ahdab narrated to us, from Mujahid, and Hajjaj said: I heard Mujahid, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I was given five not given to anyone before me: The earth was made for me pure and a mosque, and spoils were made lawful for me and were not lawful for a prophet before me, and I was aided with terror a month journey against my enemy, and I was sent to every red and black, and I was given intercession, and it will reach from my nation whoever does not associate with Allah anything; Hajjaj said: Whoever dies associating nothing with Allah."
"21766","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Mudrik, from Abu Zurah, from Kharashah ibn al-Hurr, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Three, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will not speak to them on the Day of Resurrection, nor look at them, nor purify them; he said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) read it three times; he said: So Abu Dharr said: They have failed and lost, they have failed and lost, they have failed and lost; he said: Who are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The one who drags his lower garment, and the one who reminds of his giving, and the one who promotes his goods with a false oath."
"21767","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Yahya ibn Sam, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Abu Dharr, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: When you fast three days of a month, fast the thirteenth and the fourteenth and the fifteenth."
"21768","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Mundhir al-Thawri, from elders of them, from Abu Dharr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Mundhir ibn Yala Abu Yala, from elders of his, from Abu Dharr, and he mentioned its meaning, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw two sheep butting one another, and said: O Abu Dharr, do you know for what they butt? He said: No; he said: But Allah knows, and He will judge between them."
"21769","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Mundhir al-Thawri, from elders of them, from Abu Dharr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Mundhir ibn Yala Abu Yala, from elders of his, from Abu Dharr, and he mentioned its meaning, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw two sheep butting one another, and said: O Abu Dharr, do you know for what they butt? He said: No; he said: But Allah knows, and He will judge between them."
"21770","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from al-Mundhir al-Thawri, from elders of them, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left us, and no bird flapping in the sky but he reminded us knowledge from it."
"21771","Hajjaj narrated to us, Fitr narrated to us, from al-Mundhir, from Abu Dharr, the same meaning."
"21772","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Muhajir Abu al-Hasan of Banu Taym Allah, a freedman of theirs, he said: We returned from a funeral and passed by Zayd ibn Wahb, and he narrated from Abu Dharr, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and the caller to prayer wanted to call the adhan, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cool it down, then he wanted to call the adhan, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cool it down, he said it three times; he said: Until we saw the shade of the hillocks, then he prayed, then he said: The intensity of heat is from the blaze of Hell, so when the heat is intense, cool down the prayer."
"21773","Hajjaj and Hashim narrated to us, they said: Layth narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Ibn Shimasah, that Muawiyah ibn Hudayj passed by Abu Dharr while he was standing at a horse of his, and he asked him: What are you treating of this horse of yours? So he said: I think that this horse has had its supplication answered; he said: And what is the supplication of a beast among beasts? He said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, there is no horse but it supplicates every dawn, saying: O Allah, You have entrusted me to a servant of Your servants, and made my provision in his hand, so make me more beloved to him than his family and his wealth and his child; my father said: And Amr ibn al-Harith agreed with him, from Ibn Shimasah."
"21774","Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Dhakwan, Ayyub ibn Bushayr narrated to me, from Fulan al-Anazi, and he did not say al-Ghubari, that he came with Abu Dharr, and when he returned the people dispersed from him, so I said: O Abu Dharr, I shall ask you about some affair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: If it is a secret from the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I shall not narrate to you; I said: It is not a secret, but when he met a man he would take his hand, shaking hands with him; he said: Upon an expert you have fallen; he never met me but he took my hand, except one time, and that was the last of them; he sent to me, so I came to him in his illness in which he died, and I found him lying down, so I leaned over him, and he raised his hand and embraced me (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"21775","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abu al-Husayn informed me, from Ayyub ibn Bushayr ibn Kab al-Adawi, from a man of Anazah, that he said to Abu Dharr when he was exiled from Sham, and he mentioned the hadith, and he said in it: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shake hands with you when you met him? So he said: I never met him but he shook my hand."
"21776","Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad al-Ammi narrated to us, Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, he said: I was behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when we exited the outskirts of Madinah, and he said: O Abu Dharr, pray the prayer at its time, and if you come and the imam has prayed, you have secured your prayer before that, and if you come and he has not prayed, pray with him, and your prayer will be supererogatory for you; O Abu Dharr, what if the people hunger until you cannot reach your mosque from exhaustion, or you cannot return to your bed from exhaustion, how will you do? He said: I said: Allah and His Messenger know best; he said: Be patient, O Abu Dharr; what if the people die until a house equals a slave, how will you do? He said: I said: Allah and His Messenger know best; he said: Restrain yourself; he said: O Abu Dharr, what if the people are killed until the stones of oil drown in blood, how will you do? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best; he said: Enter your house; I said: O Messenger of Allah, what if I am entered upon? He said: Come to whom you are from; he said: I said: Shall I carry a weapon? He said: Then you have shared; he said: I said: How shall I do, O Messenger of Allah? He said: If you fear that the glare of the sword dazzles you, cast an edge of your cloak over your face, he will bear your sin and his."
"21777","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Isa, from Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Dharr, and Muammil said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from his brother, from his father, from Abu Dharr, he said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about everything until I asked him about wiping the pebbles; so he said: Once, or leave; Muammil said: About leveling the pebbles or wiping."
"21778","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jurashi, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr al-Hadrami, from Abu Dharr, he said: We fasted with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Ramadan, and he did not lead us in anything of the month until seven remained, then he stood with us until near a third of the night had gone, then he did not lead us on the fourth night, and he stood with us on the night following it until near half the night had gone; he said: So we said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you had supererogated for us the rest of this night of ours; he said: When a man stands with the imam until he leaves, the rest of his night is counted for him; then he did not lead us on the sixth, and he stood with us on the seventh, and he said: And he sent to his family and the people gathered, then he stood with us until we feared that al-Falah would escape us; he said: I said: What is al-Falah? He said: The suhur."
"21779","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, and Abd al-Ala, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you stands to prayer, mercy faces him, so do not move the pebbles."
"21780","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Habib, freedman of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Urwah, from Abu Murawih al-Ghifari, from Abu Dharr, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him, saying: O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are best? He said: Faith in Allah and jihad in the cause of Allah; so he said: Which emancipation is best? He said: The most precious of it; he said: What if I do not find? He said: Then you help a craftsman or make for one lacking skill; he said: What if I cannot? He said: Then withhold your evil from the people, for it is a charity you give for yourself."
"21781","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Makhul, from a man, from Abu Dharr, he said: A man called Akkaf ibn Bishr al-Tamimi entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Akkaf, have you a wife? He said: No; he said: Nor a slave girl? He said: Nor a slave girl; he said: And you are well-off with good? He said: And I am well-off with good; he said: You are then from the brothers of the devils, and if you were among the Christians you would be among their monks; our sunnah is marriage; your worst are your unmarried, and the vilest of your dead are your unmarried; do you wrestle with Satan: Satan has no weapon more effective among the righteous than women, except the married, those are the purified, acquitted of indecency; woe to you, O Akkaf, they are the companions of Ayyub and Dawud and Yusuf and Kursuf; so Bishr ibn Atiyah said to him: And who is Kursuf, O Messenger of Allah? He said: A man who worshipped Allah on a seacoast of the seacoasts of the sea for three hundred years, fasting the day and standing the night, then he disbelieved in Allah the Almighty because of a woman he loved, and abandoned what he was upon of worship of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, then Allah remedied him with some of what was from him, and repented upon him; woe to you, O Akkaf, marry, otherwise you are from the wavering; he said: Marry me, O Messenger of Allah; he said: I have married you to Karimah bint Kulthum al-Himyari."
"21782","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn al-Numan, Abdullah ibn Yazid ibn al-Aqna al-Bahili narrated to us, al-Ahnaf ibn Qays narrated to us, he said: I was in Madinah, and there was a man from whom the people flee when they see him; he said: I said: Who are you? He said: I am Abu Dharr, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: I said: What makes the people flee? He said: I forbid them hoarding with that with which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them."
"21783","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Awzai saying: Harun ibn Riab informed me, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, he said: I entered Bayt al-Maqdis and found therein a man much in prostration, and I found in myself from that, and when he finished I said: Do you know for an even or an odd you finished? He said: If I do not know, then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, knows; then he said: My beloved Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed me, then he wept, then he said: My beloved Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed me, then he wept, then he said: My beloved Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed me that he said: There is no servant who prostrates to Allah a prostration but Allah raises him a degree by it, and removes from him a sin by it, and writes for him a good deed by it; he said: I said: Inform me who you are, may Allah have mercy on you; he said: I am Abu Dharr, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so my soul shrank to me."
"21784","Abd al-Razzaq and Yazid narrated to us, they said: Hisham narrated to us, from al-Hasan, Sasaa narrated to me, Yazid said: Ibn Muawiyah, that he met Abu Dharr while he was leading a camel of his, and in its neck was a waterskin, and I said to him: Will you not narrate to me a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There are no two Muslims whose three children die before reaching puberty but Allah admits them to Paradise by virtue of His mercy to them."
"21785","And there is no Muslim who spends a pair of his wealth in the cause of Allah but the keepers of Paradise hasten to him, and Yazid said: But Allah admits them to Paradise by virtue of His mercy to them."
"21786","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ala ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Nuaym ibn Qanab, he said: I went out to al-Rabadhah, and Abu Dharr came, and he spoke to his wife about a thing, and as if she answered him back, and he repeated and she repeated, so he said: You add nothing over what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woman is like the rib, if you bend it, it breaks, and in it is sufficiency and crookedness."
"21787","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, he said: The black dog cuts off the prayer, I think he said: And the menstruating woman; he said: I said to Abu Dharr: What is the matter with the black dog? He said: I have asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, so he said: It is a devil."
"21788","Yazid narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Jumay al-Qurashi informed us, Abu al-Tufayl Amir ibn Wathilah narrated to us, from Hudhayfah ibn Asid, he said: Abu Dharr stood and said: O Banu Ghifar, say and do not differ, for the truthful, the believed, narrated to me that the people will be gathered upon three troops: A troop riding, eating, clothed, and a troop walking and running, and a troop the angels drag upon their faces and gather them to the Fire; so one of them said: These two we have known, so what is the matter with those who walk and run? He said: Allah casts calamity upon the backs until no back remains, until a man has an admired garden and gives it for an aged camel with a saddle, and cannot afford it."
"21789","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Makhul, from Ghudayf ibn al-Harith, a man from Aylah, he said: I passed by Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he said: A good boy; so a man among those with him followed me and said: O son of my brother, supplicate Allah for me with good; he said: I said: Who are you, may Allah have mercy on you? He said: I am Abu Dharr, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so I said: May Allah forgive you, you are more entitled to supplicate for me than I for you; he said: O son of my brother, I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab, when I passed by him just now, saying: A good boy, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah has placed truth upon the tongue of Umar, he speaks with it."
"21790","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Irak ibn Malik, he said: Abu Dharr said: I am the nearest of you on the Day of Resurrection to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The nearest of you to me on the Day of Resurrection is whoever leaves the world in the state I left him upon, and by Allah, there is none of you but he has clung to it with something, except me."
"21791","Yazid narrated to us, Sufyan, meaning Ibn Husayn, narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Dharr, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon a donkey, and upon it was a saddle blanket or a velvet cloth; he said: And that was at sunset, so he said to me: O Abu Dharr, do you know where this sets? He said: I said: Allah and His Messenger know best; he said: It sets in a warm spring, proceeding until it falls to its Lord, Mighty and Majestic, prostrating beneath the Throne; and when the time of its emergence comes, Allah permits it, so it emerges and rises; and when He wants to raise it from where it sets, He withholds it, so it says: O Lord, my course is far; so He says to it: Rise from where you set; so that is when no soul its faith benefits."
"21792","Yazid and Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, they said: al-Awwam narrated to us, Muhammad said: From al-Qasim, and Yazid said in his hadith: al-Qasim ibn Awf al-Shaybani narrated to me, from a man, he said: We had carried something for Abu Dharr, wanting to give it to him, so we came to al-Rabadhah and asked about him and did not find him; it was said: He sought permission for Hajj and was permitted, so we came to him at al-Baldah, which is Mina, and while we were with him, it was said to him: Uthman prayed four; so that was hard upon Abu Dharr, and he said a harsh saying, and he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he prayed two, and I prayed with Abu Bakr and Umar, then Abu Dharr stood and prayed four; so it was said to him: You faulted the Commander of the Faithful for something then you did it; he said: Dissension is worse; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said: There will be after me authority, so do not humiliate it; so whoever wants to humiliate it has cast off the bond of Islam from his neck, and no repentance is accepted from him until he repairs his breach which he breached, and he will not do, then he returns to be among those who honour it; our Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us not to be overcome upon three: That we enjoin good and forbid evil and teach the people the sunan."
"21793","Yazid narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from Qatadah, from Said ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, he heard Abu Dharr, he said: My friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined me: Any gold or silver that is tied up is a branding upon its owner until he spends it in the cause of Allah, spending."
"21794","Yazid narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Muammil, from Qays ibn Sad, from Mujahid, from Abu Dharr, that he took hold of the ring of the door of the Kabah and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No prayer after Asr until the sun sets, nor after Fajr until the sun rises, except in Makkah, except in Makkah."
"21795","Rawh and Hashim narrated to us, they said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to us, Hashim said: From Humayd, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, he said: Abu Dharr said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man loves the people and cannot do like their deeds; he said: You, O Abu Dharr, are with whom you loved; I said: For I love Allah and His Messenger; he said: Then you, O Abu Dharr, are with whom you loved; Hashim said: He said it to him three times: You are with whom you loved."
"21796","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Habib ibn Abi Thabit and Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay and al-Amash informed me, all of them heard Zayd ibn Wahb narrating from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever dies associating nothing with Allah enters Paradise."
"21797","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Husayn, meaning al-Muallim, narrated to us, from Ibn Buraydah, Yahya ibn Yamar narrated to me, that Abu al-Aswad narrated to him, from Abu Dharr, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no man who claims for other than his father while he knows it but he disbelieves, and whoever claims what is not his is not from us, and let him take his seat in the Fire, and whoever calls a man with disbelief or says: Enemy of Allah, while it is not so, but it returns upon him."
"21798","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Husayn narrated to us, from Ibn Buraydah, that Yahya ibn Yamar narrated to him, that Abu al-Aswad al-Dili narrated to him, that Abu Dharr said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and upon him was a white garment, and he was sleeping, then I came to him to speak to him, and he was sleeping, then I came to him and he had awakened, so I sat to him, and he said: There is no servant who says: There is no god but Allah, then dies upon that, but enters Paradise; I said: Even if he commits adultery and steals? He said: Even if he commits adultery and steals; I said: Even if he commits adultery and steals? He said: Even if he commits adultery and steals, three times, then he said on the fourth: Despite the nose of Abu Dharr; he said: So Abu Dharr went out dragging his lower garment, saying: Even if the nose of Abu Dharr dislikes; he said: So Abu Dharr used to narrate with this after, saying: Even if the nose of Abu Dharr dislikes."
"21799","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibrahim, meaning Ibn al-Ashtar, from his father, that Abu Dharr death attended him while he was at al-Rabadhah, and his wife wept, so he said: What makes you weep? She said: I weep, I have no strength for yourself, and I have no garment wide enough for you as a shroud; so he said: Do not weep, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, while I was with him among a group, saying: A man from among you will surely die in a deserted land of the earth, witnessed by a company of believers; he said: So all who were with me in that gathering died in a community and division, and none of them remained except me, and I have morning in a deserted land dying, so watch the road, for you shall see what I say, for by Allah, I did not lie nor was I lied to; she said: And how is that when the Hajj has been cut off? He said: Watch the road; he said: So while she was thus, there were the people, their mounts hastening with them as if they were vultures, and the people came until they stood upon her, and said: What is with you? She said: A man from the Muslims, you shroud him and are rewarded therein; they said: And who is he? She said: Abu Dharr; so they ransomed him with their fathers and their mothers, and placed their whips in their throats, hastening to him, so he said: Rejoice, you are the group about whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said what he said; rejoice, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There are no two Muslim women between whom two or three children perish, and they reckon and are patient, but they ever see the Fire; then I have morning today as you see, and if a garment of mine were wide enough for me I would not be shrouded except in it, so I adjure you by Allah that no man among you who was a leader or a headman or a courier shroud me; so all the people had attained something of that except a youth from the Ansar who was with the people; he said: I am your companion, two garments in my bag from the spinning of my mother, and I find these two garments of mine upon me; he said: You are my companion, so shroud me."
"21800","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Ibrahim al-Taymi narrating from his father, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he asked him about the first mosque placed for the people; he said: The Sacred Mosque, then Bayt al-Maqdis; so he was asked: How many years between them? He said: Forty years; and wherever the prayer reaches you, pray, for there is a mosque."
"21801","Abd al-Razzaq told us, Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Dharr, who said: It was said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: The people of wealth have carried off the reward. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed there is much charity in you. He mentioned the merit of your hearing and the merit of your sight. He said: And in your intercourse with your wife there is charity. Abu Dharr said: Is one of us rewarded for his desire? He said: What do you think, if you had placed it in what is unlawful, would there be sin upon you? He said: Yes. He said: Do you count the evil but not count the good?"
"21802","Affan told us, Abu al-Ashhab told us, Khulayd al-Asari told us — Abu Jurayy said: Where did you meet Khulayd? He said: I do not know — from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, who said: I was sitting with some people of Quraysh when Abu Dharr came until he was near them. He said: Let the hoarders be given tidings of branding from the direction of their backs emerging from the direction of their bellies, and branding from the direction of the backs of their necks emerging from their foreheads. He said: Then he withdrew and sat. He said: I said: Who is this? He said: Abu Dharr. He said: So I stood up to him and said: What is this thing I heard you proclaiming? He said: I said nothing to them except something they have heard from their Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: I said to him: What do you say about this stipend? He said: Take it, for in it today is assistance; but if it becomes a price for your religion, then leave it."
"21803","Affan and Arim Abu al-Numan both said: Dulaym ibn Ghazwan al-Attar al-Abdi told us, Wahb ibn Abi Dubayy told us — Affan said: he told me — from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad, from Mihjan, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The evil eye indeed makes a man climb, by the permission of Allah, ascending to a high place, then he falls down from it."
"21804","Arim told us, Mahdi ibn Maymun told us, Ghaylan told us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Madi Karib, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrating it from his Lord. He said: Son of Adam, as long as you call upon Me and hope in Me, I forgive you for whatever is in you. Son of Adam, if you meet Me with sins filling the earth, I will meet you with its fill of forgiveness, after you do not associate anything with Me. Son of Adam, if you sin until your sin reaches the clouds of the sky, then you seek My forgiveness, I will forgive you and I do not care."
"21805","Arim and Affan both said: Mahdi ibn Maymun told us, Wasil the freedman of Abu Uyaynah told us, from Yahya ibn Uqayl, from Yahya ibn Yamar, from Abu al-Aswad al-Dili, from Abu Dharr, who said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, the people of riches have taken the rewards; they pray as we pray, they fast as we fast, and they give charity from the surplus of their wealth. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Has Allah not made for you that which you may give as charity? Indeed in every tasbihah there is charity, and in every tahmidah there is charity, and in the intercourse of one of you there is charity. He said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, does one of us come to his desire and there is reward for him in it? He said: What do you think, if he placed it in what is unlawful, would there be sin upon him in it? Likewise, when he places it in what is lawful, there is reward for him in it. Affan said: you give as charity, and he said: and in tahlilah and takbirah there is charity, and enjoining good is charity, and forbidding evil is charity, and in intercourse —"
"21806","Abu al-Nadr told us, Mahdi told us — and he did not mention Abu al-Aswad."
"21807","Arim and Affan both said: Mahdi ibn Maymun told us, from Wasil the freedman of Abu Uyaynah, from Yahya ibn Uqayl, from Yahya ibn Yamar, from Abu al-Aswad al-Dili, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Each morning upon every joint of one of you there is charity; every tasbihah is charity, tahlilah is charity, takbirah is charity, tahmidah is charity, enjoining good is charity, forbidding evil is charity, and sufficient for one of you from all of that are two rakahs which he prays in the forenoon."
"21808","Affan told us, Hammad ibn Salamah told us, Abu Husayn informed me, from Ayyub ibn Bushayr ibn Kab al-Adawi, from a man of Anz, that he said to Abu Dharr when he was sent away from Syria, he said: I wish to ask you about a hadith from the hadith of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Then I will inform you of it, unless it is a secret. I said: It is not a secret: did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, shake hands with you when you met him? He said: I never met him except that he shook my hand. One day he sent for me, and I was not in the house; when I came I was told of his messenger, so I went to him while he was on a couch of his, and he embraced me, and it was most excellent and most excellent."
"21809","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us, Shubah told us, he said: I heard Abu Imran al-Jawni narrating from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man does a deed for himself and people love him for it. He said: That is the hastened glad tidings of the believer."
"21810","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us, Shubah told us, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Aliyah al-Barra, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: O Abu Dharr, how will you be when you remain among a people who delay the prayer from its time? He said: He said to me: Pray the prayer at its time; if you find them not having prayed, pray with them, and do not say: I have already prayed and I will not pray."
"21811","Abu Amir told us, Shubah told us, from Budayl ibn Maysarah, he said: I heard Abu al-Aliyah al-Barra, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, struck his thigh and said to him: How will you be when you remain among a people who delay the prayer? Then he said: Pray the prayer at its time, then rise; if you are in the mosque until the prayer is established, pray with them."
"21812","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us, Shubah told us, from a man of Thaqif called Fulan ibn Abd al-Wahid, he said: I heard Abu Mujib say: Abu Dharr met Abu Hurayrah — and he made me see, he said, the scabbard of his sword was silver — and he forbade him. Abu Dharr said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no person — or he said: no one — who leaves gold or silver except that he will be branded with it."
"21813","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us, Shubah told us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Sulayman ibn Mushir, from Kharashah ibn al-Hurr, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Three to whom Allah will not speak on the Day of Resurrection, nor look at them, nor purify them, and for them is a painful punishment: the one who reminds of what he gave, the one who trails his lower garment, and the one who sells his merchandise with a false oath."
"21814","Wahb ibn Jarir told us, Mahdi ibn Maymun told us, from Wasil, from Yahya ibn Uqayl, from Yahya ibn Yamar, from Abu al-Aswad al-Dili, from Abu Dharr, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, the people of riches have taken the rewards; they pray as we pray, they fast as we fast, and they give charity from the surplus of their wealth. He said: Has Allah not made for you that which you give as charity? Indeed in every tasbihah there is charity, in every takbirah there is charity, in every tahlilah there is charity, in every tahmidah there is charity, enjoining good is charity, forbidding evil is charity, and in the intercourse of one of you there is charity. They said: O Messenger of Allah, does one of us come to his desire and there is reward for him in it? He said: What do you think, if he placed it in what is unlawful, would there not be sin upon him — or the sin? They said: Yes. He said: Likewise, when he places it in what is lawful, there is reward for him."
"21815","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr told us, Sufyan told us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Mawraq, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Those of your servants who suit you, feed them from what you eat and clothe them from what you wear — or he said: from what you acquire — and whoever does not suit you, sell them, and do not torment the creation of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"21816","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr told us, Ali — meaning Ibn Mubarak — told us, from Yahya, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from Abu Sallam. Abu Dharr said: Upon every soul, on every day in which the sun rises, there is charity due from him upon himself. I said: O Messenger of Allah, from where shall I give charity when we have no wealth? He said: Because among the doors of charity are: takbir, and Subhan Allah, and al-hamdu lillah, and la ilaha illa Allah, and astaghfirullah, and you enjoin good and forbid evil, and you remove the thorn from the path of the people, and the bone and the stone, and you guide the blind, and you make the deaf and the mute hear until they understand, and you direct one seeking guidance to a need of his whose place you know, and you hasten with the strength of your legs to the distressed one seeking help, and you lift with the strength of your arms with the weak — all of that is among the doors of charity from you upon yourself. And for you in your intercourse with your wife there is reward. Abu Dharr said: How can there be reward for me in my desire? The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What do you think, if you had a child, and he grew up and you hoped for his good, then he died — would you count it? I said: Yes. He said: Did you create him? He said: Rather Allah created him. He said: Did you guide him? He said: Rather Allah guided him. He said: Did you provide for him? He said: Rather Allah used to provide for him. He said: Likewise, place it in what is lawful and keep it away from what is unlawful; if Allah wills He gives it life, and if He wills He causes it to die, and for you there is reward."
"21817","Affan told us, Hammad ibn Salamah told us, Abu Naamah informed us, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, who said: I came to Madinah wanting the stipend from Uthman ibn Affan, and I sat with a circle of the circles of Quraysh, when a man came wearing worn garments, having wrapped a cloth upon his head. He said: Give tidings to the hoarders of branding on the foreheads, and branding on the backs, and branding on the sides. Then he withdrew to a pillar and prayed two rakahs behind it. I said: Who is this? It was said: This is Abu Dharr. I said to him: What is this thing I heard you proclaiming? He said: I said to them nothing except something they heard from their Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. I said: May Allah have mercy on you, I used to take the stipend from Umar; what do you think? He said: Take it, for in it today there is assistance, and it is about to become a debt; when it becomes a debt, then refuse it."
"21818","Abu Kamil told us, Hammad told us, Abu Naamah al-Saadi told us — and he mentioned it with its isnad and meaning — and he did not mention except: something they heard from their Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. And I do not think Affan except that he erred and went to the hadith of Abu al-Ashhab, for Affan added it, and it was not with us."
"21819","Abu Muawiyah told us, al-Amash told us, from Shimr ibn Atiyah, from his elders, from Abu Dharr, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: When you do an evil deed, follow it with a good deed; it will efface it. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, is la ilaha illa Allah among the good deeds? He said: It is the best of good deeds."
"21820","He told us."
"21821","Ibn Numayr told us, al-Ajlah told us, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from Abu al-Aswad al-Dili, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best of that with which gray hair is changed is henna and katam."
"21822","Ismail told us, Salih ibn Rustum told us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Abdullah ibn Samit, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: O Abu Dharr, there will be rulers over you who delay the prayer from its fixed times; if you reach their time, pray the prayer at its time — and perhaps he said: in your dwelling — then go to them; if you find them having prayed, you have already prayed, and if you find them not having prayed, pray with them, and it will be voluntary for you."
"21823","Abu Muawiyah told us, al-Amash told us, from al-Marur ibn Suwayd, from Abu Dharr, who said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was sitting in the shade of the Kabah. When he saw me approaching, he said: They are the greatest losers, by the Lord of the Kabah. I said: What is wrong with me? Perhaps something has been revealed about me. Who are they, may my father and mother be ransom for you? He said: Those with the most wealth, except one who says thus — and he scattered before him and to his right and to his left. He said: Then he said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, none of you dies leaving camels, cattle, or sheep of which he did not pay the zakah, except that it will come to him on the Day of Resurrection greater and fatter than it was, trampling him with its hooves and butting him with its horns; whenever the last of them passes over him, the first of them is brought back, until judgment is passed among the people."
"21824","Abu Muawiyah told us, al-Amash told us, from al-Marur ibn Suwayd, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I know the last of the people of the Fire to come out of the Fire, and the last of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise: a man will be brought, and it will be said: Put aside his major sins and question him about his minor ones. He said: It will be said to him: You did such-and-such on such-and-such day, and you did such-and-such on such-and-such day. He said: He will say: O Lord, I did things I do not see here. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, laughed until his molars appeared. He said: It will be said to him: For you, in place of every evil deed, a good deed."
"21825","Abu Muawiyah told us, al-Amash told us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Abu Dharr, raise your sight and look at the highest man you see in the mosque. He said: I looked, and there was a man sitting wearing a fine suit. He said: I said: This one. He said: O Abu Dharr, raise your sight and look at the lowest man you see in the mosque. I looked, and there was a weak man wearing worn clothes. He said: I said: This one. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, this one is better with Allah on the Day of Resurrection than the earth full of the like of this one."
"21826","Yahya ibn Said told us, from Yahya ibn Said: Abu Salih told me, from a man of Banu Asad, from Abu Dharr, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The most intense of my ummah in love for me are a people who will be — or will come — after me; one of them would wish that he had given his family and his wealth and that he had seen me."
"21827","Yahya told us, Qudamah ibn Abdullah told us, Jasrah bint Dajajah told me that she set out to perform umrah and reached al-Rabadhah, where she heard Abu Dharr say: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood one night among the nights in the Isha prayer and led the people in prayer, then some companions of his stayed behind praying. When he saw their standing and their staying behind, he left to his dwelling; when he saw that the people had vacated the place, he returned to his place and prayed. I came and stood behind him, and he gestured to me with his right hand, so I stood on his right. Then Ibn Masud came and stood behind me and behind him, and he gestured to him with his left hand, so he stood on his left. We three stood, each man of us praying by himself and reciting of the Quran whatever Allah willed him to recite. He stood with a verse of the Quran repeating it until he prayed the dawn. After we entered the morning, I gestured to Abdullah ibn Masud to ask him what he intended by what he did last night. Ibn Masud said with his hand: I will not ask him about anything until he speaks to me. I said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, you stood with a verse of the Quran while you have the Quran with you; if one of us did this, we would hold it against him. He said: I supplicated for my ummah. He said: What was answered to you, or what was replied to you? He said: I was answered with that which, if many of them were to behold it a single beholding, they would abandon prayer. He said: Shall I not give the people glad tidings? He said: Yes. So I set out hastening, near a stone's throw, when Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, if you send to the people with this, they will fall back from worship. So he called out that he return, and he returned. That verse is: If You punish them, they are Your servants; but if You forgive them, indeed You are the Exalted in Might, the Wise."
"21828","Marwan told us, Qudamah al-Bakri told us — and he mentioned the like of it — and he said: they fall back from worship."
"21829","Yahya ibn Said told us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar: Yazid ibn Abi Habib told me, from Suwayd ibn Qays, from Muawiyah ibn Hudayj, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no Arabian horse except that it is permitted, with every dawn, to supplicate with two supplications, saying: O Allah, You have entrusted me to those whom You entrusted me of the sons of Adam, so make me among the most beloved of his family and wealth to him — or: the most beloved of his family and wealth to him. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: My father said: Amr ibn al-Harith differed from him and said: from Yazid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimashah. And Layth said: from Abu Shimashah as well."
"21830","Yahya ibn Said told us, from Yazid ibn Ibrahim: Qatadah told us, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, who said: I said to Abu Dharr: Had I seen the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I would have asked him. He said: About what? I said: I would ask him: Did Muhammad see his Lord? He said: I asked him, and he said: Light — how could I see Him?"
"21831","Yahya ibn Said told us, from Ikrimah ibn Ammar: Abu Zumayl Simak al-Hanafi told me, Malik ibn Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Zimmani told me, my father Marthad told me, he said: I asked Abu Dharr, I said: You had asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about Laylat al-Qadr. He said: I was the most questioning of the people about it. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me about Laylat al-Qadr: is it in Ramadan or in other than it? He said: Rather it is in Ramadan. He said: I said: Is it with the prophets as long as they live, and when they are taken it is lifted, or is it until the Day of Resurrection? He said: Rather it is until the Day of Resurrection. He said: I said: In which Ramadan is it? He said: Seek it in the first ten or the last ten. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, spoke, and spoke; then I seized an opportunity and caught him unawares. I said: In which of the twenty is it? He said: Seek it in the last ten; do not ask me about anything after it. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, spoke, and spoke; then I seized an opportunity and caught him unawares, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I adjure you by my right upon you to inform me in which of the ten it is. He said: He became angry with me with an anger the like of which he had not been angry with since I accompanied him — a wording like it. He said: Seek it in the last seven; do not ask me about anything after it."
"21832","Yahya ibn Said told us, Hisham told us, my father told me that Abu Murawih al-Ghifari informed him that Abu Dharr informed him that he said: O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best? He said: Faith in Allah and jihad in His path. He said: Which necks are best? He said: The most expensive in price and the most precious to its people. He said: What if I do not do it? He said: You help a craftsman or make for one lacking skill. He said: What if I am weak? He said: You withhold from evil, for it is charity you give as charity upon yourself."
"21833","Yahya ibn Said told us, from Shubah: Abu Imran al-Jawni told us, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, who said: When Abu Dharr came to Uthman from Syria, he said: My close friend, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded me with three: Hear and obey, even if an Abyssinian slave with mutilated limbs; when you make broth, increase its water, then look at a household among your neighbors and give them thereof in kindness; and pray the prayer at its time, for if you find the imam has prayed, you have secured your prayer, otherwise it is voluntary."
"21834","Makki ibn Ibrahim told us, Abdullah ibn Abi Ziyad told us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from a cousin of Abu Dharr, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever drinks wine, Allah will not accept his prayer for forty nights; if he repents, Allah turns to him; if he returns, it is the same. I do not know whether in the third or in the fourth, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If he returns, it becomes incumbent upon Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, to give him to drink of the mud of khabal. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the mud of khabal? He said: The exudation of the people of the Fire."
"21835","Yahya ibn Ghaylan told us, Rishdin — meaning Ibn Sad — told us, Amr ibn al-Harith told me. He said: And Rishdin told me, from Salim ibn Ghaylan al-Tujibi, he told him that Sulayman ibn Abi Uthman told him, from Hatim ibn Adi — or Adi ibn Hatim al-Himsi — from Abu Dharr, who said: I said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: I wish to stay overnight with you tonight and pray with your prayer. He said: You cannot bear my prayer. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood to wash, screening himself with a garment while I turned away from him; he washed, then I did the like of that. Then he stood praying, and I stood with him, until I began striking my head against the walls from the length of his prayer. Then Bilal called the adhan for prayer. He said: Did you do it? He said: Yes. He said: O Bilal, you call the adhan when the morning is shining in the sky, and that is not the morning; the morning is thus, spread wide. Then he called for sahur and took sahur."
"21836","Affan told us, Abu Awanah told us, from Abu Bishr, from Talq ibn Habib, from Bushayr ibn Kab al-Adawi, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Shall you have a treasure from the treasures of Paradise? He said: I said: Yes. He said: La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah."
"21837","Affan told us, Hammam told us, Amir al-Ahwal told us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Madi Karib, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in what he narrates from his Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, that He said: O son of Adam, as long as you call upon Me and hope in Me, I shall forgive you for whatever is in you; were you to meet Me with sins filling the earth, I would meet you with its fill of forgiveness; were you to do sins until they reach the clouds of the sky, as long as you do not associate anything with Me, then you sought My forgiveness, I would forgive you, then I do not care."
"21838","Affan told us, Mahdi ibn Maymun told us, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Madi Karib, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"21839","Musa ibn Dawud told us, Ibn Lahiah told us, from Salim ibn Ghaylan, from Sulayman ibn Abi Uthman, from Adi ibn Hatim al-Himsi, from Abu Dharr, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Bilal: You, O Bilal, call the adhan when the morning is shining in the sky, but that is not the morning; the morning is thus, spread wide. Then he called for his sahur and took sahur. And he used to say: My ummah will remain in good as long as they delay the sahur and hasten the breaking of the fast."
"21840","Ali ibn Ishaq told us, he said: Abdullah said: Yunus told me, from al-Zuhri, he said: I heard Abu al-Ahwas, the freedman of Banu Layth, narrating to us in the gathering of Ibn al-Musayyab, while Ibn al-Musayyab was sitting, that he heard Abu Dharr say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, remains facing the servant in his prayer as long as he does not turn; when he turns his face away, He turns away from him."
"21841","Abu al-Mughirah told us, Safwan told us, from Abu al-Yaman and Abu al-Muthanna, that Abu Dharr said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took my pledge for five, and bound me to seven, and called Allah to witness over me nine: that I not fear in Allah the blame of any blamer. Abu al-Muthanna said: Abu Dharr said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called me and said: Will you pledge, and for you is Paradise? I said: Yes, and I extended my hand. The Messenger of Allah said, stipulating upon me: that you not ask people for anything. I said: Yes. He said: Not even your whip, if it falls from you, until you dismount to it and take it."
"21842","Abu al-Yaman told us, Safwan ibn Amr told us, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd al-Hadrami, referring it to Abu Dharr, that he said: When the last ten came, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, secluded himself in the mosque. When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed the Asr prayer of the twenty-second day, he said: We shall stand tonight, if Allah wills; whoever of you wishes to stand, let him stand — and it is the night of the twenty-third. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed it in congregation after the night prayer until a third of the night had gone, then he left. When it was the night of the twenty-fourth, he did not pray anything and did not stand. When it was the night of the twenty-fifth, he stood after the Asr prayer of the twenty-fourth day and said: We shall stand tonight, if Allah wills — meaning the night of the twenty-fifth — whoever wishes, let him stand. He prayed with the people until a third of the night had gone, then he left. When it was the night of the twenty-sixth, he said nothing and did not stand. When it was at the Asr prayer of the twenty-sixth day, he stood and said: We shall stand, if Allah wills — meaning the night of the twenty-seventh — whoever wishes to stand, let him stand. Abu Dharr said: We braced ourselves for standing, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with us until two-thirds of the night had gone, then he left to his dome in the mosque. I said to him: We had hoped, O Messenger of Allah, that you would stand with us until morning. He said: O Abu Dharr, when you pray with your imam and leave when he leaves, there is written for you the devotion of your night. Abu Abd al-Rahman said."
"21843","Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad told us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, Layth informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Marwan, from al-Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, from Abu Dharr, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was sitting while two sheep were butting one another; one of them butted the other and caused it to miscarry. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, laughed. It was said to him: What makes you laugh, O Messenger of Allah? He said: I marvel at her. By the One in whose hand is my soul, retribution will surely be taken for her on the Day of Resurrection."
"21844","Hasan told us, Ibn Lahiah told us, Huyayy ibn Abdullah told us that Abu Kathir, the freedman of Banu Hashim, told him that he heard Abu Dharr al-Ghifari, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Words — whoever mentions them one hundred times after every prayer: Allahu Akbar, Subhan Allah, al-hamdu lillah, la ilaha illa Allah alone without partner, and la hawla wa la quwwata illa billah — then even if his sins were like the foam of the sea, they would be effaced. My father said: He did not raise it."
"21845","Hasan told us, Ibn Lahiah told us, al-Harith ibn Yazid told us, he said: I heard Ibn Hujayrah the elder say: One who heard Abu Dharr informed me, saying: I conversed privately with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, through the night until dawn, and said: O Messenger of Allah, appoint me. He said: It is a trust, and disgrace and regret on the Day of Resurrection, except for one who takes it by its right and fulfills what is due upon him in it."
"21846","Hasan told us, Ibn Lahiah told us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib told us that Abu Salim al-Jayshani came to Abu Umayyah in his dwelling and said: I heard Abu Dharr say that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: When one of you loves his companion, let him come to him in his dwelling and inform him that he loves him for Allah, the Mighty and Majestic. I have loved you, so I have come to you in your dwelling."
"21847","Ibn al-Walid told us, Sufyan told us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Mawraq al-Ijli, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Those of your servants who suit you, feed them from what you eat and clothe them from what you wear; and those of your servants who do not suit you, sell them, and do not torment the creation of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"21848","Aswad — he is Ibn Amir — told us, Israil told us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Mujahid, from Mawraq, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I see what you do not see and hear what you do not hear. The sky has groaned, and it has the right to groan: there is not in it the space of four fingers except upon it an angel prostrating. If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much, you would not enjoy women on beds, and you would go out to the high roads crying out to Allah. He said: Abu Dharr said: By Allah, I wish I were a tree that is cut down."
"21849","Al-Hakam ibn Musa told us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Rijal al-Madani told us, Umar the freedman of Ghufr informed us, from Ibn Kab, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: My beloved enjoined upon me five: to have mercy on the poor and sit with them, to look at one below me and not look at one above me, to join the ties of kinship even if it turns away, to speak the truth even if it is bitter, and to say la hawla wa la quwwata illa billah. The freedman of Ghufr says: I do not know there remains with us of the five except this: our saying la hawla wa la quwwata illa billah."
"21850","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And I heard it from al-Hakam ibn Musa — and he said: from Muhammad ibn Kab, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"21851","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi told us, Ismail — meaning Ibn Jafar — informed us, Muhammad ibn Abi Harmalah informed me, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Dharr, who said: My beloved enjoined upon me three which I shall never abandon, if Allah wills, ever: he enjoined upon me the Duha prayer, and the witr before sleep, and fasting three days of every month."
"21852","Rawh told us, Abu Amir al-Khazzaz told us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Do not belittle anything of good; if you find nothing, meet your brother with a cheerful face."
"21853","Wahb ibn Jarir told us, my father told us, he said: I heard Harmalah narrating from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimashah, from Abu Basrah, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You will conquer Egypt, and it is a land in which the qirat is named; when you conquer it, be good to its people, for they have protection and kinship — or he said: protection and marriage ties. If you see two men disputing in it over the place of a brick, leave it. He said: I saw Abd al-Rahman ibn Shurahbil Ibn Hasanah and his brother Rabiah disputing over the place of a brick, so I left it."
"21854","He said: And Harun told it to us: Ibn Wahb told us, Harmalah told us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimashah, he said: I heard Abu Dharr — and he mentioned its meaning."
"21855","Sulayman ibn Dawud Abu Dawud told us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban told us, my father told me, from Makhul, from Ibn Abi Nuaym, he told him, from Usamah ibn Salman, that Abu Dharr told them that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, says: Allah accepts the repentance of His servant — or forgives His servant — as long as the veil has not fallen. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the veil? He said: That the soul dies while associating partners."
"21856","Zayd ibn al-Hubab told us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban told us, from his father, from Makhul, from Umar ibn Nuaym, from Usamah ibn Salman, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, forgives His servant as long as the veil has not fallen. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the falling of the veil? He said: That the soul dies while associating partners."
"21857","Ali ibn Ayyash and Isam ibn Khalid both said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban told us, from his father, from Makhul, from Umar ibn Nuaym, from Usamah ibn Salman — and Isam said: Umar ibn Nuaym al-Ansi — that Abu Dharr told them, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the falling of the veil? That the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, forgives His servant — and they mentioned the like of it."
"21858","Yazid ibn Harun told us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah informed us, Humayd ibn Hilal told us, from Abdullah ibn Samit, who said: Abu Dharr said: We left our people Ghifar — and they used to permit the sacred month — I, my brother Unays, and our mother. We set out until we alighted upon a maternal uncle of ours, a man of wealth and standing. Our uncle honored us and treated us well, but his people envied us. They said: When you leave your family, Unays succeeds you to them. Our uncle came to us and repeated to him what was said to him. I said: As for what has passed of your kindness, you have spoiled it, and we shall have no union in what is after. He said: We brought near our camel herd and loaded upon it; our uncle covered himself with his garment and began to weep. He said: We set out until we alighted near Makkah. He said: Unays boasted against a man concerning our herd and the like of it, and they went to the soothsayer, who gave judgment for Unays. He brought us our herd and the like of it. I had prayed, O son of my brother, before meeting the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for three years. He said: I said: To whom? He said: To Allah. He said: I said: In which direction? He said: Wherever Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, directed me. He said: I would pray the night prayer until, when it was the end of the night, I would fall as though a cover, until the sun rose over me. He said: Unays said: I have a need in Makkah; suffice me until I come to you. He said: He set out and was delayed from me, then came to me. I said: What detained you? He said: I met a man claiming that Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, sent him upon your religion. He said: I said: What do the people say to him? He said: They say he is a poet, a magician, a soothsayer. Unays was a poet. He said: I have heard the speech of the soothsayers, and his speech is not theirs; I have set his speech against the measures of poetry, and by Allah no tongue can fit it as poetry. By Allah he is truthful and they are liars. He said: I said to him: Will you suffice me until I go and see? He said: Yes, but beware of the people of Makkah, for they have become hostile to him and stern toward him. He said: I set out until I came to Makkah, and I made light of a man among them. I said: Where is this man whom you call the Sabian? He said: He pointed at me, saying: The Sabian. He said: The people of the valley turned upon me with every clod and bone until I fell unconscious. I rose when I rose as though a red idol. I came to Zamzam, drank of its water, washed the blood from me, and entered between the Kabah and its curtains. I remained there, O son of my brother, thirty days and nights, with no food except the water of Zamzam; I grew fat until the folds of my belly broke, and I found no leanness of hunger upon my liver. He said: While the people of Makkah were on a moonlit bright night, Allah struck upon the ears of the people of Makkah, and none circumambulated the House except two women. They came upon me supplicating Isaf and Nailah. He said: I said: Marry one of them to the other. That did not restrain them. He said: They came upon me again, and I said a coarse word like a piece of wood, except that I did not use a euphemism. They went off wailing, saying: Were there here any of our men. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, met them, he and Abu Bakr, descending from the mountain. He said: What is wrong with you? They said: The Sabian is between the Kabah and its curtains. They said: What did he say to you? They said: He said to us a word that fills the mouth. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came, he and his companion, until he touched the Stone and circumambulated the House, then prayed. He said: I went to him, and I was the first to greet him with the greeting of Islam. He said: Upon you, and the mercy of Allah. From whom are you? He said: I said: From Ghifar. He said: He motioned with his hand and placed it upon his forehead. He said: I said to myself: He disliked that I ascribed myself to Ghifar. He said: I wanted to take his hand, but his companion restrained me, and he knew him better than I. He said: When were you here? He said: I have been here for thirty days and nights. He said: Who was feeding you? I said: I had no food except the water of Zamzam; I grew fat until the folds of my belly broke, and I found no leanness of hunger upon my liver. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is blessed; it is food that nourishes. Abu Bakr said: Permit me, O Messenger of Allah, in his food tonight. He said: He did. He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, set out, Abu Bakr set out, and I set out with them, until Abu Bakr opened a door and began to take handfuls for us of the raisins of Taif. That was the first food I ate there. I remained as I remained; then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I have been directed to a land of date palms, and I think it is none but Yathrib. Will you convey from me to your people? Perhaps Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will benefit them through you and reward you for them. He said: I set out until I came to Unays. He said: He said to me: What did you do? He said: I said: I have submitted and believed. He said: He said: I have no aversion to your religion; I have submitted and believed. Then we came to our mother, and she said: I have no aversion to your religion; I have submitted and believed. We loaded up until we came to our people Ghifar. Some of them submitted before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Madinah, and some of them said: When he comes. Their imam was Khufaf ibn Ima ibn Rahdah al-Ghifari, and he was their chief that day. The rest of them said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, comes, we shall submit. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Madinah, and the rest of them submitted. He said: Aslam came and said: O Messenger of Allah, our brothers — we submit upon that which they submitted. So they submitted. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Ghifar — may Allah forgive her; and Aslam — may Allah grant her peace."
"21859","Abdullah told us, Hudbah told us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah told us — and he mentioned the like of it with its isnad."
"21860","Yazid — meaning Ibn Harun — told us, Yazid ibn Ibrahim told us, Qatadah told us, Abdullah ibn Shaqiq told us, he said: I said to Abu Dharr: Had I reached the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I would have asked him. He said: About what would you have asked him? He said: I would have asked him: Did he see his Lord, the Mighty and Majestic? Abu Dharr said: I asked him, and he said: Light — how could I see Him?"
"21861","Yazid told us, Hammam informed us, from Qatadah, from Said ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Samit, who said: I was with Abu Dharr when his stipend came out, and with him was a slave girl of his who used to attend to his needs — and once he said: we attend — and there remained with him a surplus; I think he said: seven. He ordered her to buy small coins with it. I said: O Abu Dharr, had you saved it for a need that befalls you and for a guest who comes to you? He said: My close friend enjoined upon me that whatever gold or silver is tied up is a live coal upon its owner on the Day of Resurrection, until he pours it out pouring in the path of Allah."
"21862","Yazid told us, al-Jurayri Abu Masud informed us, from Abu Abdullah al-Jasri, from Ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which speech is most beloved to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic? He said: That which He chose for His angels: Subhan Allah wa bihamdih — three times you say it."
"21863","Yazid told us, al-Aswad ibn Shayban informed us, from Yazid Abu al-Ala, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, who said: A hadith reached me from Abu Dharr, and I wished to meet him. I met him and said to him: O Abu Dharr, a hadith reached me from you, and I wished to meet you and ask you about it. He said: You have met, so ask. He said: I said: It reached me that you say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Three whom Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, loves, and three whom Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, hates. He said: Yes; I do not think I lie against my close friend Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him — three times he said it. He said: I said: Who are the three whom Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, loves? He said: A man who campaigns in the path of Allah, meeting the enemy striving and seeking reward, fighting until he is killed — and you find in the Book of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: Indeed Allah loves those who fight in His path in ranks; and a man with a neighbor who harms him, who bears his harm and counts it, until Allah suffices him against him by death or life; and a man with a people traveling until sleep or slumber weighs upon them, and they alight at the end of the night, and he rises to his ablution and his prayer. He said: I said: Who are the three whom Allah hates? He said: The boastful arrogant — and you find in the Book of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: Indeed Allah does not love every arrogant boaster; and the miserly giver of reminders; and the merchant, the seller given to swearing. He said: I said: O Abu Dharr, what is wealth? He said: A firq for us and a dhawd — meaning by firq a few sheep. He said: I said: I am not asking about this; I ask you about solid wealth. He said: What is in the morning is not in the evening, and what is in the evening is not in the morning. He said: I said: O Abu Dharr, what is with you and your brothers of Quraysh? He said: By Allah, I shall not ask them for worldly gain nor seek their fatwa about the religion of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, until I meet Allah and His Messenger — three times he said it."
"21864","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us, Shubah told us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: There are people of my ummah whose mark is shaving; they recite the Quran, it does not pass beyond their throats; they pass out of the religion as the arrow passes out of the game. They are the worst of creation and creatures."
"21865","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us, Shubah told us, from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Suwayd ibn al-Harith, he said: I heard Abu Dharr say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I do not love that I have the like of Uhud in gold — Shubah said: or he said: I do not love that Uhud be gold for me — leaving of it, on the day I die, a dinar or half a dinar, except for a creditor."
"21866","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us, Shubah told us, he said: I heard Muhajir Abu al-Hasan narrating that he heard Zayd ibn Wahb narrating from Abu Dharr, who said: The caller to prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called the adhan for Zuhr. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Cool it, cool it — or he said: Wait, wait. He said: The intensity of heat is from the exhalation of Hell; when the heat is intense, cool the prayer. Abu Dharr said: Until we saw the shade of the mounds."
"21867","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi told us, Sufyan told us, from al-Mughirah ibn al-Numan, from Abdullah ibn Yazid ibn al-Aqna, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, who said: While I was in a circle, Abu Dharr came, and they began to flee from him. I said: Why do people flee from you? He said: I forbid them hoarding, which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to forbid them."
"21868","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi told us, Shubah told us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Aslam — may Allah grant her peace; and Ghifar — may Allah, Blessed and Exalted, forgive her."
"21869","Yahya ibn Said told us, from Sufyan: Habib told me, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Fear Allah wherever you are, mix with people with good character, and when you do an evil deed, do a good deed; it will efface it."
"21870","Yahya told us, from Fitr: Yahya ibn Sam told me, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us to fast the thirteenth, the fourteenth, and the fifteenth."
"21871","Yahya told us, from Fitr: Yahya ibn Sam told me, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us to fast the thirteenth, the fourteenth, and the fifteenth."
"21872","Yahya told us, from Ibn Ajlan: Sad told me, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Wadiah, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever washes — or purifies himself — and perfects the purification, wears of his best clothes, touches of the perfume or oil of his family what Allah has written for him, then comes to Friday, does not engage in idle talk and does not separate between two, he is forgiven what is between it and the next Friday."
"21873","Ibn Numayr told us, Musa — meaning Ibn al-Musayyab al-Thaqafi — told us, from Shahr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm al-Ashari, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: O My servants, all of you are sinful except whom I preserve; so seek My forgiveness, I shall forgive you. Whoever among you knows that I have power over forgiveness and seeks My forgiveness by My power, I forgive him and I do not care. All of you are astray except whom I guide; so ask Me for guidance, I shall guide you. All of you are poor except whom I enrich; so ask Me, I shall provide for you. Were your living and your dead, your first and your last, your moist and your dry, to gather upon the heart of the most Godfearing servant among My servants, they would not increase in My dominion the wing of a gnat. Were your living and your dead, your first and your last, your moist and your dry, to gather, and every asker among them asked what his wish amounts to, and I gave every asker what he asked, it would not diminish Me except as when one of you passes by the shore of the sea and dips a needle then pulls it out. That is because I am Generous, Glorious, Self-sufficient; I do whatever I will. My giving is speech and My punishment is speech: when I intend a thing, I only say to it: Be, and it is."
"21874","Ibn Numayr and Muhammad ibn Ubayd both said: Al-Amash told us, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, who said: Abu Dharr said: While I was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the mosque when the sun set, he said: O Abu Dharr, where does the sun go? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: It goes until it prostrates before its Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, then seeks permission, and permission is given to it; it is as though it has been said to it: Return from whence you came, and it rises from its place — and that is its resting place. Muhammad said: Then he recited: And the sun runs to its resting place."
"21875","Yala ibn Ubayd told us, Muhammad — meaning Ibn Ishaq — told us, from Makhul, from Ghudayf ibn al-Harith, who said: I passed by Umar with a group of his companions; a man among them caught up with me and said: O youth, supplicate Allah for me with good; may Allah bless you. He said: I said: Who are you, may Allah have mercy on you? He said: I am Abu Dharr. He said: I said: May Allah forgive you; you are more deserving. He said: I heard Umar say: An excellent youth; and I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has placed the truth upon the tongue of Umar; he speaks by it."
"21876","Waki told us, al-Amash told us, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Dharr, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the saying of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: And the sun runs to its resting place. He said: Its resting place is beneath the Throne."
"21877","Waki told us, al-Masudi told us, from Ali ibn Mudrik, from Kharashah ibn al-Hurr, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Three to whom Allah will not speak, nor look at them on the Day of Resurrection, nor purify them, and for them is a painful punishment: the one who trails, the giver of reminders, and the one who sells his merchandise with a wicked oath."
"21878","Waki told us, Israil told us, from Jabir, from Thabit ibn Sad — or Said — from Abu Dharr, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stoned a woman, and commanded me to dig for her; I dug for her up to my navel."
"21879","Waki told us, al-Masudi told us, Abu Umar al-Dimashqi informed me, from Ubayd ibn al-Khashkhash, from Abu Dharr, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in the mosque, and sat. He said: O Abu Dharr, have you prayed? I said: No. He said: Stand and pray. He said: I stood and prayed, then sat. He said: O Abu Dharr, seek refuge in Allah from the evil of the devils of men and jinn. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, are there devils among men? He said: Yes. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what of prayer? He said: Placed good; whoever wills, less, and whoever wills, more. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what of fasting? He said: An obligatory duty that suffices, and with Allah is increase. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what of charity? He said: Multiples multiplied. I said: O Messenger of Allah, which of them is best? He said: The effort of one of little, or a secret to a poor one. I said: O Messenger of Allah, which of the prophets was first? He said: Adam. I said: O Messenger of Allah, and was he a prophet? He said: Yes, a prophet spoken to. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how many are the messengers? He said: Three hundred and some ten, a great multitude — and once he said: fifteen. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, was Adam a prophet? He said: Yes, a prophet spoken to. I said: O Messenger of Allah, which of what was revealed to you is greatest? He said: Ayat al-Kursi: Allah, there is no god but He, the Living, the Sustainer."
"21880","Waki told us, from Sufyan: Yazid — meaning Ibn Abi Ziyad — told us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abu Dharr, who said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, the hyenas have eaten us. He said: Other than that is more fearful to me for you than that: that the world be poured upon you pouring; would that my ummah not wear gold."
"21881","Yazid told us, Hisham informed us, from Wasil, from Yahya ibn Uqayl, from Yahya ibn Yamar, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Each day, upon every joint of the son of Adam there is charity. Then he said: Your removing harm from the path is charity, your greeting people is charity, your enjoining good is charity, your forbidding evil is charity, and your intercourse with your wife is charity. He said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, does a man fulfill his desire and there is charity for him? He said: Yes. What do you think, had he placed that desire in what Allah forbade him, would there not be sin upon him? We said: Yes. He said: When he places it in what Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, permitted, it is charity. He said: And he mentioned things: charity, charity. He said: Then he said: Sufficient from all of this are the two rakahs of Duha."
"21882","Affan told us, Mahdi told us, Wasil told us, from Yahya ibn Uqayl, from Yahya ibn Yamar — Wasil would sometimes mention Abu al-Aswad al-Dili — from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The deeds of my ummah were presented to me, its good and its bad; I found among the good of its deeds the harm removed from the path, and I found among the bad of its deeds the spittle in the mosque not buried."
"21883","Yazid told us, Hisham informed us, from Wasil, from Yahya ibn Uqayl, from Yahya ibn Yamar, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: My ummah was presented to me with its deeds, good and bad; I saw among the good of its deeds the removal of harm from the path, and I saw among the bad of its deeds the spittle in the mosque not buried."
"21884","Yazid told us, Kahmas ibn al-Hasan told us, Abu al-Salil told us, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, kept reciting to me this verse: And whoever fears Allah, He makes for him a way out — until he finished the verse. Then he said: O Abu Dharr, had all people taken by it, it would have sufficed them. He said: He kept reciting it and repeating it to me until I dozed. Then he said: O Abu Dharr, what will you do if you are expelled from Madinah? He said: I said: To ease and comfort — I shall go until I am a dove among the doves of Makkah. He said: What will you do if you are expelled from Makkah? He said: I said: To ease and comfort — to Syria and the holy land. He said: And what will you do if you are expelled from Syria? He said: I said: Then, by the One who sent you with the truth, I shall place my sword upon my shoulder. He said: Is there better than that? He said: I said: Is there better than that? He said: You hear and obey, even if an Abyssinian slave."
"21885","Yazid told us, al-Masudi informed us, from Abu Amr al-Shami, from Ubayd ibn al-Khashkhash, from Abu Dharr, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in the mosque, and sat to him. He said: O Abu Dharr, have you prayed? I said: No. He said: Stand and pray. He said: I stood and prayed, then came to him and sat to him. He said to me: O Abu Dharr, seek refuge in Allah from the evil of the devils of men and jinn. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, are there devils among men? He said: Yes. O Abu Dharr, shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise? He said: I said: Yes, may my father and mother be ransom for you. He said: Say: La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah, for it is a treasure from the treasures of Paradise. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what of prayer? He said: Placed good; whoever wills, more, and whoever wills, less. He said: I said: What of fasting, O Messenger of Allah? He said: An obligatory duty that suffices. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what of charity? He said: Multiples multiplied, and with Allah is increase. He said: I said: Which is best, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The effort of one of little, or a secret to a poor one. I said: Which of what Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed to you is greatest? He said: Allah, there is no god but He, the Living, the Sustainer — until he completed the verse. I said: Which of the prophets was first? He said: Adam. I said: And was he a prophet, O Messenger of Allah? He said: A prophet spoken to. I said: How many are the messengers, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Three hundred and fifteen, a great multitude."
"21886","Yazid told us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you stands to prayer, mercy faces him; so let him not touch the pebbles nor move them."
"21887","Yazid told us, Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn al-Mughirah al-Taifi, from Abdullah ibn al-Miqdam, from Ibn Shaddad, from Abu Dharr, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, when a man came to him and said: The other has committed adultery. He turned away from him, then a second, then a third, then a fourth. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, alighted once, and he confessed to him of adultery; he turned him back four times. Then he alighted and commanded us; we dug for him a pit not deep, and he was stoned. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, departed gloomy and grieved. We traveled until we alighted at a stop, and it was relieved from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said to me: O Abu Dharr, did you not see your companion? He was forgiven and admitted to Paradise."
"21888","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us, Awf told us, from Muhajir Abu Khalid: Abu al-Aliyah told me, Abu Muslim told me, he said: I said to Abu Dharr: Which standing of the night is best? Abu Dharr said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as you asked me — Awf doubts — and he said: The middle of the night that has passed — or half the night — and few are its doers."
"21889","Abu Amir told us, Abd al-Jalil — meaning Ibn Atiyah — told us, Muzahim ibn Muawiyah al-Dabbi told us, from Abu Dharr, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out in winter while leaves were falling. He took two branches of a tree. He said: Those leaves began to fall. He said: He said: O Abu Dharr. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The Muslim servant prays the prayer seeking thereby the face of Allah, and his sins fall from him as these leaves fall from this tree."
"21890","Muhammad ibn Bakr told us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Imran ibn Abi Anas — it reached him from him — from Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan al-Nadri, from Abu Dharr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Upon camels is their charity, upon sheep is their charity, upon cattle is their charity, and upon wheat is its charity."
"21891","Yahya ibn Adam and Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr, the freedman of al-Bara — and he praised him well — both said: Zuhayr told us, from Mutarrif — Ibn Abi Bukayr said: Mutarrif — meaning al-Harithi — told us — from Abu al-Jahm — Ibn Abi Bukayr said: from Khalid ibn Wuhban — or Wuhban — from Abu Dharr, who said: He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: How will you be with rulers after me who appropriate this fay? He said: I said: Then, by the One who sent you with the truth, I shall place my sword upon my shoulder, then strike with it until I meet you or join you. He said: Shall I not guide you to what is better than that? Be patient until you meet me."
"21892","Abdullah told us, my father told me, Abu Jafar Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub told us, Abu Bakr — meaning Ibn Ayyash — told us, from Mutarrif, from Abu al-Jahm, from Khalid ibn Wuhban, from Abu Dharr, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Abu Dharr, how will you be with rulers who appropriate against you this fay? He said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I shall place my sword upon my shoulder and strike with it until I join you. He said: Shall I not guide you to better for you than that? Be patient until you meet me."
"21893","Abdullah told us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad told us, Abu Bakr — meaning Ibn Ayyash — told us, from Mutarrif, from Abu al-Jahm, from Khalid ibn Wuhban, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever departs from the congregation a span removes the yoke of Islam from his neck."
"21894","Yahya ibn Adam told us, Zuhayr told us, from Mutarrif ibn Tarif, from Abu al-Jahm, from Khalid ibn Wuhban, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever separates from the congregation a span removes the yoke of Islam from his neck."
"21895","Aswad ibn Amir told us, Abu Bakr told us, from Mutarrif, from Abu al-Jahm, from Khalid ibn Wuhban, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said — and he mentioned the like of it."
"21896","Abu Abd al-Rahman told us, Said ibn Abi Ayyub told us, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar told me, from Salim ibn Abi Salim al-Jayshani, from his father, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Abu Dharr, do not take charge of the wealth of an orphan, and do not command over two."
"21897","Hajjaj told us, Shayban told us, Mansur told us, from Ribi, from Kharashah ibn al-Hurr, from al-Marur, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was given the closing verses of Surat al-Baqarah from a treasure beneath the Throne, and no prophet before me was given them."
"21898","Hashim told us, Shayban told us, from Asim, from al-Marur ibn Suwayd, from Abu Dharr, who said: The truthful one believed told me — raising the hadith. He said: The good deed is ten or more, and the evil deed is one, or I forgive it. Whoever meets Me not associating anything with Me, with sins filling the earth, I make for him the like of it in forgiveness."
"21899","Zayd ibn al-Hubab told us, Muawiyah ibn Salih told us, Abu al-Zahiriyyah told me, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Abu Dharr, who said: We stood with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the night of the twenty-third in the month of Ramadan until the first third of the night. Then he said: I think what you seek is only behind you. Then we stood with him on the night of the twenty-fifth until half the night. Then he said: I think what you seek is only behind you. We stood with him on the night of the twenty-seventh until morning, and he was silent."
"21900","Wahb ibn Jarir, Arim, and Yunus said: Mahdi ibn Maymun told us, from Wasil the freedman of Abu Uyaynah — Arim said: Wasil told us — from Yahya ibn Uqayl, from Yahya ibn Yamar, from Abu al-Aswad al-Dili, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The deeds of my ummah were presented to me, its good and its bad; I found among the good of its deeds the removal of harm from the path, and I found among the bad of its deeds the spittle — Arim said: in the mosque not buried; and Yunus said: the spittle in the mosque not buried."
"21901","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Amr ibn Bujdan, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Pure earth is the ablution of the Muslim, even if he does not find water for ten years, then when he finds it let him touch it to his skin, for that is better."
"21902","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ajlan, from Said ibn Abi Said, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Wadiah, from Abu Dharr, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever bathes on Friday and performs the bath well, then wears some of his good clothes, then touches some of his household oil, what is decreed, or some of his perfume, then does not separate between two, Allah expiates for him what is between it and Friday. Muhammad said: So I mentioned to Ubadah ibn Amir ibn Amr ibn Hazm: He spoke the truth, and the addition of three days."
"21903","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, and I heard it myself from Harun, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith ibn Yaqub informed me, from his father, from Abu al-Aswad al-Ghifari, from al-Numan al-Ghifari, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: O Abu Dharr, comprehend what I say to you: a suckling kid goat coming to a Muslim man is better for him than Uhud in gold that he leaves behind him. O Abu Dharr, comprehend what I say to you: Indeed those who have much are the fewest on the Day of Resurrection, except one who says such-and-such and such-and-such. Comprehend, O Abu Dharr, what I say to you: Indeed good is in the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection, or: Indeed good is in the forelocks of horses."
"21904","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Husayn narrated to me, he said: Ibn Buraydah said: Yahya ibn Yamar narrated to me that Abu al-Aswad narrated to him, from Abu Dharr, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: No man accuses a man of fisq, nor accuses him of kufr, except it returns upon him, if his companion is not so."
"21905","Yahya ibn Ishaq informed us, Ibn Luhayah and Musa, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Ubayd ibn Abi Jafar, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Any man who lifts a curtain and lets his sight enter before he is given permission has committed a violation it is not lawful for him to commit, and if a man were to gouge his eye it would be void, and if a man were to pass by a door that has no curtain and see the nakedness of its people, there is no sin upon him; the sin is only upon the people of the house."
"21906","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, Darraj narrated to us, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Dharr, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Six days, then comprehend, O Abu Dharr, what I say to you afterwards. Then when it was the seventh day he said: I enjoin upon you fear of Allah in your secret affair and your open, and when you do evil then do good, and do not ask anyone for anything even if your whip falls, and do not take custody of a trust, and do not judge between two."
"21907","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr and from Darraj, from Abu al-Muthanna, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Six days, comprehend, O Abu Dharr, what is said to you, except that he said: And do not shelter a trust, and do not judge between two."
"21908","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mahdi al-Ubuli narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Wasil, freedman of Abu Uyaynah, from Yahya ibn Aqil, from Yahya ibn Yamar, from Abu al-Aswad al-Dili, he said: I saw the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I did not see one resembling Abu Dharr. Last of the hadith of Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him."
